pang International Circuit  Kuala Lumpur   \n","2          3      bahrain   Bahrain International Circuit        Sakhir   \n","3          4    catalunya  Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya      Montmeló   \n","4          5     istanbul                   Istanbul Park      Istanbul   \n","\n","     country       lat        lng  alt  \\\n","0  Australia -37.84970  144.96800   10   \n","1   Malaysia   2.76083  101.73800   18   \n","2    Bahrain  26.03250   50.51060    7   \n","3      Spain  41.57000    2.26111  109   \n","4     Turkey  40.95170   29.40500  130   \n","\n","                                                 url  \n","0  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melbourne_Grand_P...  \n","1  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sepang_Internatio...  \n","2  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bahrain_Internati...  \n","3  http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circuit_de_Barcel...  \n","4         http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Istanbul_Park  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["df = raw[\"circuits\"]\n","df.info()\n","display(df.head())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"da060671","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.020301,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.699023+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.678722+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**circuits** has one row per circuit, 77 in total, describing where races are held:\n","\n","- **circuitId:** the number that identifies each circuit. Other tables (we expect `races`) use it to say where a race took place.\n","- **circuitRef:** a short text name for the circuit (e.g. `albert_park`), another identifier.\n","- **name:** the full official name of the circuit.\n","- **location:** the city or area where the circuit is (e.g. Melbourne).\n","- **country:** the country of the circuit, written as a country name (e.g. Australia, Spain).\n","- **lat / lng:** the circuit's geographic coordinates.\n","- **alt:** the circuit's altitude, in metres, above sea level.\n","- **url:** the circuit's Wikipedia page.\n","\n","**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Types:** `lat` and `lng` were read as decimal numbers (`float64`), and `alt` and `circuitId` as whole numbers (`int64`). pandas stores a whole column as text (`object`) if even one value in it is not a number, such as the `\\N` placeholder. Since these four columns came out as numbers, none of them contains a placeholder. The non-null counts in `.info()` are all 77, but at this stage that does not mean nothing is missing: we loaded the data without letting pandas mark anything as missing, so a `\\N` is counted as a normal value. The audit (1.2) counts the placeholders directly.\n","\n","2) **country** is the column that matters most here. Data-engineering Question 2 compares races in a driver's home country with races elsewhere. In the rows shown, countries are written as names (Australia, Spain, Turkey). The F1 introduction mentions that drivers' nationality is stored differently, as an adjective such as \"British\". We check this when we reach `drivers`; if the two are written differently, we will need a mapping between them for Question 2.\n","\n","3) **circuitId** is needed for Question 1, which asks at which circuits a front-row start (grid 1 or 2) most often turns into a podium. To answer it, we compute that rate separately for each circuit, so every result must be linked to the circuit where the race took place, through `circuitId`.\n","\n","4) **Available before the race?** Yes. A circuit is a fixed fact about the race known long in advance, so nothing in this table is leakage. `lat`, `lng`, `alt`, `url` and `circuitRef` are descriptive and not needed for any of our questions."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"21417d27","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.02094,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.741573+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.720633+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**How are countries written?** The first rows only show 5 of the 77 circuits. Since Question 2 depends on matching circuit countries to driver nationalities, each country has to be written in exactly one way: if the same country appeared under two different names, it would be counted as two separate countries. We list every distinct value to check."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"eebb2cea","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.784387Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.784075Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.790399Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.789287Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.030237,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.792405+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.762168+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["35 different country values\n","['Argentina', 'Australia', 'Austria', 'Azerbaijan', 'Bahrain', 'Belgium', 'Brazil', 'Canada', 'China', 'France', 'Germany', 'Hungary', 'India', 'Italy', 'Japan', 'Korea', 'Malaysia', 'Mexico', 'Monaco', 'Morocco', 'Netherlands', 'Portugal', 'Qatar', 'Russia', 'Saudi Arabia', 'Singapore', 'South Africa', 'Spain', 'Sweden', 'Switzerland', 'Turkey', 'UAE', 'UK', 'USA', 'United States']\n"]}],"source":["print(df[\"country\"].nunique(), \"different country values\")\n","print(sorted(df[\"country\"].unique()))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"027ed0e9","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.020804,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.833585+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.812781+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["There are 35 distinct country values, and the United States appears under two labels: `USA` and `United States`. Grouping by country as it stands would split the US into two countries. Most countries are written as full names, but a few use short forms (`UK`, `UAE`). `UK` is also the form the F1 introduction uses as its example. We look at which circuits carry each of the two US labels."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"0106446f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.878366Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.877278Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.896437Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.895315Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.044195,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.898609+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.854414+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>circuitId</th>\n","      <th>name</th>\n","      <th>location</th>\n","      <th>country</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>18</th>\n","      <td>19</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis Motor Speedway</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>22</th>\n","      <td>80</td>\n","      <td>Las Vegas Strip Street Circuit</td>\n","      <td>Las Vegas</td>\n","      <td>United States</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>32</th>\n","      <td>33</td>\n","      <td>Phoenix street circuit</td>\n","      <td>Phoenix</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>36</th>\n","      <td>37</td>\n","      <td>Detroit Street Circuit</td>\n","      <td>Detroit</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>41</th>\n","      <td>42</td>\n","      <td>Fair Park</td>\n","      <td>Dallas</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>42</th>\n","      <td>43</td>\n","      <td>Long Beach</td>\n","      <td>California</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>43</th>\n","      <td>44</td>\n","      <td>Las Vegas Street Circuit</td>\n","      <td>Nevada</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>45</th>\n","      <td>46</td>\n","      <td>Watkins Glen</td>\n","      <td>New York State</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>59</th>\n","      <td>60</td>\n","      <td>Riverside International Raceway</td>\n","      <td>California</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>62</th>\n","      <td>63</td>\n","      <td>Sebring International Raceway</td>\n","      <td>Florida</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>68</th>\n","      <td>69</td>\n","      <td>Circuit of the Americas</td>\n","      <td>Austin</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>76</th>\n","      <td>79</td>\n","      <td>Miami International Autodrome</td>\n","      <td>Miami</td>\n","      <td>USA</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["    circuitId                             name        location        country\n","18         19      Indianapolis Motor Speedway    Indianapolis            USA\n","22         80   Las Vegas Strip Street Circuit       Las Vegas  United States\n","32         33           Phoenix street circuit         Phoenix            USA\n","36         37           Detroit Street Circuit         Detroit            USA\n","41         42                        Fair Park          Dallas            USA\n","42         43                       Long Beach      California            USA\n","43         44         Las Vegas Street Circuit          Nevada            USA\n","45         46                     Watkins Glen  New York State            USA\n","59         60  Riverside International Raceway      California            USA\n","62         63    Sebring International Raceway         Florida            USA\n","68         69          Circuit of the Americas          Austin            USA\n","76         79    Miami International Autodrome           Miami            USA"]},"execution_count":4,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["df[df[\"country\"].isin([\"USA\", \"United States\"])][[\"circuitId\", \"name\", \"location\", \"country\"]]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5ede9fe2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.021001,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.940276+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.919275+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["The US has 12 circuits in the data. Eleven are labelled `USA`; only one, the Las Vegas Strip Street Circuit (circuitId 80), is labelled `United States`. The inconsistency therefore comes from a single circuit, and in cleaning (1.8) we relabel it as `USA`, the form used by all the other US circuits. Without this, Question 2 would treat races at this circuit as being in a different country from every other US race.\n","\n","The `location` column is not consistent either: for some circuits it gives a city (Detroit, Austin, Miami), for others a whole state (California, Nevada, Florida). This does not affect our work. Question 1 identifies circuits by `circuitId` and Question 2 matches drivers to circuits by `country`, so `location` is not used anywhere and we leave it as it is.\n","\n","The list also includes the Indianapolis Motor Speedway (circuitId 19), home of the Indianapolis 500. According to the F1 introduction, this American race counted in the F1 championship from 1950 to 1960 even though almost no regular F1 drivers took part, which would distort Question 2 on home races, so excluding it is a defensible choice. The races themselves are listed in the `races` table, so we come back to this there."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e4c8c080","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.020914,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.981958+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:16.961044+00:00","status":"completed"},"tag