otal:\n","\n","- **constructorId:** the number that identifies each constructor. Other tables use it to say which team a driver raced for.\n","- **constructorRef:** a short text name for the team (e.g. `toro_rosso`), another identifier.\n","- **name:** the team's name (e.g. McLaren, BMW Sauber).\n","- **nationality:** the team's nationality, written as an adjective (British, German, French, Italian).\n","- **url:** the team's Wikipedia page.\n","\n","**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Types:** only `constructorId` was read as a number (`int64`). The other four columns are text (`object`), which is expected since they hold names and links. For text columns, the type cannot tell us whether a `\\N` is hidden inside; the audit checks that.\n","\n","2) **212 constructors** is far more than the ten or so teams on a modern grid. This fits the F1 introduction's description of earlier eras, with many privately entered cars, and of teams changing names when they are sold (e.g. Toleman became Benetton, then Renault, Lotus and Alpine). According to the introduction, each name gets its own `constructorId`, so a team's history breaks at every rename. A constructor form feature built from `constructorId` will therefore restart at each rename; we accept this and note it as a limitation.\n","\n","3) **constructorId** is needed for Question 3, which compares mechanical-retirement rates between constructors, and `name` lets us report the answer with readable team names.\n","\n","4) **nationality** is written as an adjective (\"British\"), while circuits used country names (\"UK\"). Question 2 is about the driver's home country, not the team's, so this column is not needed.\n","\n","5) **Available before the race?** Yes. Which team a constructor is does not change during a race, so nothing in this table is leakage. `constructorRef` and `url` are descriptive and not needed for any of our questions."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5902f69c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022069,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.138031+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.115962+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1.1.3 **drivers**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"95d2fc3d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.18079Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.180305Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.201017Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.19999Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.045185,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.203561+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.158376+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\n","RangeIndex: 861 entries, 0 to 860\n","Data columns (total 9 columns):\n"," #   Column       Non-Null Count  Dtype \n","---  ------       --------------  ----- \n"," 0   driverId     861 non-null    int64 \n"," 1   driverRef    861 non-null    object\n"," 2   number       861 non-null    object\n"," 3   code         861 non-null    object\n"," 4   forename     861 non-null    object\n"," 5   surname      861 non-null    object\n"," 6   dob          861 non-null    object\n"," 7   nationality  861 non-null    object\n"," 8   url          861 non-null    object\n","dtypes: int64(1), object(8)\n","memory usage: 60.7+ KB\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>driverId</th>\n","      <th>driverRef</th>\n","      <th>number</th>\n","      <th>code</th>\n","      <th>forename</th>\n","      <th>surname</th>\n","      <th>dob</th>\n","      <th>