86f66","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.021602,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.978647+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:17.957045+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["`races` has one row per race, 1,125 in total:\n","\n","- **raceId:** the number that identifies each race. Most other tables use it to say which race a row belongs to.\n","- **year:** the season the race belongs to.\n","- **round:** the race's position in that season (1 = first race of the year).\n","- **circuitId:** where the race was held (points to `circuits`).\n","- **name:** the name of the Grand Prix (e.g. Australian Grand Prix).\n","- **date / time:** the day the race was held and its start time, both stored as text.\n","- **url:** the race's Wikipedia page.\n","- **fp1–fp3, quali, sprint (_date / _time):** the dates and times of the practice, qualifying and sprint sessions of that weekend.\n","\n","**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Types:** `raceId`, `year`, `round` and `circuitId` are whole numbers, so they contain no placeholder. `date` and `time` are stored as text and need converting to real dates and times in cleaning (semantic typing).\n","\n","2) **IDs are not in time order:** `raceId = 1` is the 2009 Australian Grand Prix, not a race from 1950. Like the row order of `seasons`, the IDs say nothing about time, so anything that depends on earlier races must be ordered by `date` (or `year` and `round`), never by `raceId`.\n","\n","3) **Session columns:** all ten practice, qualifying and sprint date/time columns are `\\N` for these 2009 races. Our guess is that they were only recorded for recent seasons, which the audit will measure. They only describe the weekend's schedule, so we do not need them.\n","\n","4) **This table gives every race its time and place:** `year` and `date` place each race in history, which we need for the era comparisons in Questions 1 and 3 and for splitting the data by season; `circuitId` gives its location, which Questions 1 and 2 need. The brief notes that these questions need multi-hop joins rather than `results` alone, and `races` is where this information is stored; how the other tables reach it is checked in 1.6.\n","\n","5) **Available before the race?** Yes. The date, circuit and round of a race are fixed long in advance."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":12,"id":"168f67ad","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.026367Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.025743Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.040079Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.038975Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.041799,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.04248+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.000681+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>raceId</th>\n","      <th>year</th>\n","      <th>name</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>834</th>\n","      <td>835</td>\n","      <td>1950</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis 500</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>825</th>\n","      <td>826</td>\n","      <td>1951</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis 500</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>817</th>\n","      <td>818</td>\n","      <td>1952</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis 500</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>808</th>\n","      <td>809</td>\n","      <td>1953</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis 500</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>799</th>\n","      <td>800</td>\n","      <td>1954</td>\n","      <td>Indianapolis 500</td>\n","    </tr>