d":"e2c83131","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.024292,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.979568+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:18.955276+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["10,953 of the 26,759 rows (41%) have no official `position`, far too many to build our target on. In these rows `positionText` holds the letter codes the F1 introduction describes: R (retired, 8,897), F (failed to qualify, 1,368), W (withdrawn, 336), N (not classified, 190), D (disqualified, 151) and E (excluded, 9). `positionOrder`, meanwhile, still gives every driver a rank: the driver who started 2nd and retired is ranked 9th. This confirms why our target uses `positionOrder`.\n","\n","The F and W rows are drivers who never started the race; how to handle them is decided in the scope filters (1.8). The check also shows two inconsistent rows, where `positionText` is a number (11 and 14) but `position` is `\\N`. They do not affect our target, which uses `positionOrder`, so we only note them."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"fb4b43c6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023895,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.026279+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.002384+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**How often does each reason for ending a race occur?** `status` lists 139 possible reasons, but not how often each one happens. We attach the reason in words to every result row and plot the most common ones."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"id":"b756c318","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.074623Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.074282Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.533957Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.532997Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.486249,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.536203+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.049954+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows before and after the join: 26759 26759\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# attach the status text to every result (results -> status through statusId)\n","res_status = df.merge(raw[\"status\"], on=\"statusId\", how=\"left\")\n","print(\"Rows before and after the join:\", len(df), len(res_status))\n","\n","top = res_status[\"status\"].value_counts().head(20)\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 6))\n","top.sort_values().plot(kind=\"barh\", ax=ax)\n","ax.set_title(\"The 20 most common reasons a driver's race ended\")\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"number of result rows\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"79d63497","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023499,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.583017+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.559518+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["The join kept all 26,759 rows, so every result has exactly one reason attached.\n","\n","Three things stand out. First, finishing dominates: `Finished` is the most common status and `+1 Lap` the second, ahead of every retirement reason, with `+2` to `+5 Laps` also in the top 20. Treating lapped drivers as retirements would therefore misclassify one of the largest groups in the data. Second, the most common retirement reason is `Engine`, followed by both crashes (`Accident`, `Collision`, `Spun off`) and other car failures (`Gearbox`, `Suspension`, `Transmission`, `Electrical`, `Brakes`, `Clutch`), so mechanical retirements are frequent enough for Question 3 to compare constructors meaningfully. Third, non-starters (`Did not qualify`, `Did not prequalify`, `Withdrew`) form a visible group, which we handle in the scope filters.\n","\n","The reasons we found hard to classify, such as `Collision damage` and `Retired`, do not appear in the top 20, so each is rarer than the 20th reason shown. How we assign them in Question 3 can therefore only have a small effect on its answer, although we recheck this for the 2014–2024 seasons the question covers."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f4f2fc67","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.022761,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.628424+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.605663+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Do `qualifying` and `results` agree on each driver's team?** Both tables record a `constructorId` for every driver in a race. We will later combine them through the race and the driver, so we check whether the team recorded for the same driver in the same race is the same in both."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"fecf84a6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.676339Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.675791Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.698223Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.697317Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.04907,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.700177+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:19.651107+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Pairs compared: 10494\n","Pairs with a different team: 10\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>raceId</th>\n","      <th>driverId</th>\n","      <th>constructorId_quali</th>\n","      <th>constructorId_result</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>6499</th>\n","      <td>937</td>\n","      <td>829</td>\n","      <td>206</td>\n","      <td>209</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  