ached to a race are the standings *after* it, and using them to predict that same race would be leakage.\n","\n","3) **How to use them safely:** to predict a race, we take each driver's standings from the previous race, which are known before the race starts. The F1 introduction calls this shifting standings to \"standings before this race\". Used this way, they show how well a driver has done in the season so far, which makes them a good candidate for a form feature in Section 3.\n","\n","4) **More rows than `results`:** this table has 34,863 rows, while `results` has 26,759. So some drivers appear in the standings of races they did not enter, probably because a driver keeps a place in the championship even when they miss a race. We keep this in mind when attaching standings to result rows in Section 3."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"19d3dcb7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.025908,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.130433+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.104525+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1.1.12 **constructor_standings**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":24,"id":"bd8cdff5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.185096Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.184286Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.203732Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.202605Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.049252,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.205976+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.156724+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\n","RangeIndex: 13391 entries, 0 to 13390\n","Data columns (total 7 columns):\n"," #   Column                  Non-Null Count  Dtype  \n","---  ------                  --------------  -----  \n"," 0   constructorStandingsId  13391 non-null  int64  \n"," 1   raceId                  13391 non-null  int64  \n"," 2   constructorId          