 9, 5, 2) are exactly the points in `constructor_results` for that race, and constructor 1's 14 points are the sum of its two drivers' points in `results` (10 + 4). The ranks also follow the points (9 points is 2nd, 8 points is 3rd). So these are again the standings *after* the race, and to use them we take each team's standings from the previous race.\n","\n","3) **Usefulness:** shifted this way, they describe how well a team has done in the season so far. Since the F1 introduction names car performance as the dominant factor in most eras, a team's standing before the race is a strong candidate for a constructor form feature in Section 3. The introduction also notes that the constructors' championship only started in 1958, so we expect no constructor standings before then."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f319e33b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.024903,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.304522+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.279619+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1.1.13 **lap_times**"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":25,"id":"31d8e8bf","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.360123Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.358454Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.415495Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.414385Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.086817,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.41741+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.330593+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["<class 'pandas.core.frame.DataFrame'>\n","RangeIndex: 589081 entries, 0 to 589080\n","Data columns (total 6 columns):\n"," #   Column        Non-Null Count   Dtype \n","---  ------        --------------   ----- \n"," 0   raceId        589081 non-null  int64 \n"," 1   driverId      589081 non-null  int64 \n"," 2   lap           589081 non-null  int64 \n"," 3   position      589081 non-null  int64 \n"," 4   time       