he race and the driver the row belongs to.\n","- **stop:** which stop it was for that driver (1 = first stop).\n","- **lap:** the lap on which the stop was made.\n","- **time:** the time of day when the stop happened (e.g. `17:05:23`).\n","- **duration:** how long the stop took, in seconds, written as text (`26.898`).\n","- **milliseconds:** the same duration as one number (26,898 ms).\n","\n","**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **No ID column:** like `lap_times`, a row is identified by a combination, here race, driver and stop number, which we check in the key audit (1.6).\n","\n","2) **\"time\" means something different in every table:** here it is a time of day, while in `results` it was a total race time or a gap to the winner, and in `qualifying` and `lap_times` a lap time. Columns with the same name therefore cannot all be converted the same way in cleaning; each has to be typed by what it means.\n","\n","3) **Types:** `duration` looks like a plain number of seconds but is stored as text, so at least one value somewhere is not a plain number; the audit will show it. `milliseconds` holds the same information as a whole number for every row.\n","\n","4) **Available before the race?** No. Pit stops happen during the race, and the brief explicitly lists them as not allowed as features. We do not use this table for features or for the three questions."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3129b226","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023612,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.677763+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.654151+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Summary of 1.1\n","\n","We explored all 14 tables. The table below summarises what each one holds, whether its information is known before the race starts, and what we use it for.\n","\n","| Table | What it holds | Known before the race? | What we use it for |\n","|---|---|---|---|\n","| circuits | One row per circuit | Yes | Q1 (by circuit), Q2 (circuit country) |\n","| constructors | One row per team | Yes | Q3 and constructor features, always by `constructorId` |\n","| drivers | One row per driver | Yes | Q2 (nationality); date of birth as a possible age feature |\n","| seasons | One row per year | Yes | Not used |\n","| status | Reasons a race ended | No | Q3 (mechanical retirements), identifying non-starters |\n","| races | One row per race: year, round, date, circuit | Yes | Time order, eras, data split, link to circuits |\n","| qualifying | Qualifying position and lap times | Yes (our cutoff) | Features, Q1 (qualifying vs grid); covers only 494 of 1,125 races |\n","| sprint_results | Sprint race results | Yes | Not used: only 18 races, all from 2021 |\n","| results | Each driver's race: grid, finish, points, status | Only the IDs and `grid` | Target (`positionOrder ≤ 3`), grid feature, past races for form |\n","| constructor_results | Team points per race | Only for earlier races | Possible constructor form |\n","| driver_standings | Driver championship after each race | Only if shifted to the previous race | Driver form feature |\n","| constructor_standings | Team championship after each race | Only if shifted to the previous race | Constructor form feature; none before 1958 |\n","| lap_times | Every lap of every driver | No | Not used (time conversion check only) |\n","| pit_stops | Every pit stop | No | Not used |\n","\n","**What we carry into the next steps**\n","\n","1) **Placeholders:** missing values are written as `\\N`, and in some columns as empty text; both must be treated as missing.\n","2) **Time order:** neither row order nor IDs follow time, so anything based on earlier races must be sorted by `date` (or `year` and `round`).\n","3) **Leakage:** standings and result columns describe the race they belong to, so they can only be used from earlier races.\n","4) **Joining:** `qualifying` and `results` are combined on `raceId` and `driverId` only, and a driver's team is taken from `results`.\n","5) **Fixes for cleaning:** `United States` → `USA`, `Argentinian ` → `Argentine`.\n","6) **Rows to decide on:** duplicated drivers in the same race (shared drives), drivers who never started, and the Indianapolis 500 (to be selected by name, not by circuit)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2d7dec51","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.023524,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.725382+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.701858+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1.2 Pre-Cleaning Audit\n","\n","In 1.1 we saw placeholders in many tables: `\\N` in most of them, and empty values in `qualifying.q2` and `q3`. Here we measure them in every column of every table at once. The audit is written as a function so that exactly the same measurement can be repeated after cleaning (Part C) and the two compared."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":27,"id":"19cfa688","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.775118Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.774714Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:21.062452Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:21.061374Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.314993,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:21.064414+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:20.749421+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Columns with missing values: 30 of 120\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>table</th>\n","      <th>column</th>\n","      <th>n_sentinel</th>\n","      <th>n_empty</th>\n","      <th>n_nan</th>\n","      <th>pct_missing</th>\n","    </tr>\n"