gs.driverId → drivers.driverId   34863        0   \n","19                    lap_times.raceId → races.raceId  589081        0   \n","20              lap_times.driverId → drivers.driverId  589081        0   \n","21                    pit_stops.raceId → races.raceId   11371        0   \n","22              pit_stops.driverId → drivers.driverId   11371        0   \n","\n","    orphans  pass  \n","0         0  True  \n","1         0  True  \n","2         0  True  \n","3         0  True  \n","4         0  True  \n","5         0  True  \n","6         0  True  \n","7         0  True  \n","8         0  True  \n","9         0  True  \n","10        0  True  \n","11        0  True  \n","12        0  True  \n","13        0  True  \n","14        0  True  \n","15        0  True  \n","16        0  True  \n","17        0  True  \n","18        0  True  \n","19        0  True  \n","20        0  True  \n","21        0  True  \n","22        0  True  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# (table, column, table it points to, column it points to)\n","FOREIGN_KEYS = [(\"races\", \"year\", \"seasons\", \"year\"),\n","                (\"races\", \"circuitId\", \"circuits\", \"circuitId\")]\n","for table in [\"qualifying\", \"sprint_results\", \"results\"]:\n","    FOREIGN_KEYS += [(table, \"raceId\", \"races\", \"raceId\"),\n","                     (table, \"driverId\", \"drivers\", \"driverId\"),\n","                     (table, \"constructorId\", \"constructors\", \"constructorId\")]\n","for table in [\"sprint_results\", \"results\"]:\n","    FOREIGN_KEYS += [(table, \"statusId\", \"status\", \"statusId\")]\n","for table in [\"constructor_results\", \"constructor_standings\"]:\n","    FOREIGN_KEYS += [(table, \"raceId\", \"races\", \"raceId\"),\n","                     (table, \"constructorId\", \"constructors\", \"constructorId\")]\n","for table in [\"driver_standings\", \"lap_times\", \"pit_stops\"]:\n","    FOREIGN_KEYS += [(table, \"raceId\", \"races\", \"raceId\"),\n","                     (table, \"driverId\", \"drivers\", \"driverId\")]\n","\n","fk_rows = []\n","for table, col, ref_table, ref_col in FOREIGN_KEYS:\n","    values = clean[table][col]\n","    n_missing = values.isna().sum()\n","    n_orphans = (values.notna() & ~values.isin(clean[ref_table][ref_col])).sum()\n","    fk_rows.append({\"link\": f\"{table}.{col} → {ref_table}.{ref_col}\", \"rows\": len(values),\n","                    \"missing\": n_missing, \"orphans\": n_orphans,\n","                    \"pass\": n_missing == 0 and n_orphans == 0})\n","fk_check = pd.DataFrame(fk_rows)\n","\n","print(\"Foreign keys:\", fk_check[\"pass\"].sum(), \"of\", len(fk_check), \"pass\")\n","display(fk_check)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"237d24ef","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.032015,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.624062+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.592047+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Every primary key is unique and complete:** all 14 tables pass, including the two combined keys of `lap_times` and `pit_stops`. Every row can be identified, and a join on these IDs will not copy rows.\n","2) **Every foreign key reconciles:** all 23 links pass, with no missing values and no orphans. Every result, qualifying entry, standing, lap and pit stop points to a race, driver, team and status that exist, so joins on these IDs will not lose information.\n","\n","**What we do next:** in 1.7 we turn to the 85 driver-race pairs from plot 5 and choose which row to keep for each driver in each race."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d44360e3","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.028887,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.686402+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.657515+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1.7 One row per driver per race\n","\n","Our modeling table needs exactly one row per (`raceId`, `driverId`), because each row is one prediction. Plot 5 in 1.3 found 176 rows in `results` that share their (`raceId`, `driverId`) with another row: 85 driver-race pairs in total. The brief and the F1 introduction explain where they come from: until 1957 a team could hand a car to another driver mid-race, so a driver who drove two cars in one race has two result rows, one per car.\n","\n","The brief asks us to choose a rule for which row to keep. Before choosing, we look at what these rows contain. The rule must use only information known before the race, so we do not want to pick a row by its result.\n","\n","**Did the driver start this car?** `grid` is a pre-race value, and each grid slot belongs to one car. If two drivers in the same race have the same non-zero grid, they shared that car and only one of them started it. So for every duplicated row we count how many drivers in that race have the same grid position."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":44,"id":"26eb6b92","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.748725Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.748237Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.824551Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.823391Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.110744,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.826815+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:26.716071+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows: 176 | pairs: 85 | seasons: 1950 - 1978\n","\n","Rows per pair: {2: 79, 3: 6}\n","\n","Row types:\n","row_type\n","shared slot    115\n","own slot        55\n","grid 0           6\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n","\n","'Own slot' rows per pair:\n","row_type\n","0    31\n","1    53\n","2     1\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        t