after 26580 | removed 56\n","Same finishing place twice in one race, left: 0\n","Duplicated (raceId, driverId) left: 0\n"]}],"source":["rows_before = len(clean[\"results\"])\n","clean[\"results\"] = clean[\"results\"][~clean[\"results\"][\"resultId\"].isin(same_car[\"resultId\"])].copy()\n","\n","print(\"Rows: before\", rows_before, \"| after\", len(clean[\"results\"]), \"| removed\", rows_before - len(clean[\"results\"]))\n","print(\"Same finishing place twice in one race, left:\", clean[\"results\"].duplicated([\"raceId\", \"positionOrder\"]).sum())\n","print(\"Duplicated (raceId, driverId) left:\", clean[\"results\"].duplicated([\"raceId\", \"driverId\"]).sum())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0a443bd7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.030385,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.503087+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.472702+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **56 rows removed:** 26,636 → 26,580, exactly the two rows of each of the 28 cars.\n","2) **Every car now appears once per race:** no finishing place appears twice in the same race, and still no driver appears twice.\n","\n","**What we do next:** the table has one row per driver per race, but not every row is a driver who started the race. In 1.8 we decide which rows belong in the analysis."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"96ced592","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.03177,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.564576+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.532806+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1.8 Scope filters and label fixes\n","\n","Some rows in `results` are not predictions we would ever make. The F1 introduction asks us to decide whether drivers who did not (pre-)qualify belong in the modeling table, and 1.1 raised three more issues. This step handles all of them:\n","\n","1) **Drivers who never started:** `positionText` F (failed to qualify) and W (withdrawn). At our cutoff, after qualifying and before the start, we already know these drivers will not race, so there is nothing to predict. Before removing them we check two things: that F and W agree with the `status` column, and what the 9 E (excluded) rows are, since 1.1 left them open.\n","2) **The Indianapolis 500 (1950–1960):** the F1 introduction describes it as a separate American race that almost no F1 regulars entered, which distorts the home-race question. 1.1 showed that the same circuit also hosted 8 real US Grands Prix (2000–2007), so we remove it by race name, not by circuit.\n","3) **Two labels written in two ways:** `United States` → `USA` in `circuits.country`, and `Argentinian ` (with a trailing space) → `Argentine` in `drivers.nationality`. Both matter for Question 2, which matches drivers to their home circuits.\n","\n","First, the non-starters."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":48,"id":"1c88b903","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.625027Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.624644Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.694107Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.692022Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.102184,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.696247+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.594063+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Status of the F, W and E rows:\n","positionText        E     F    W\n","status                          \n","107% Rule           0     9    0\n","Accident            0     0   29\n","Brakes              0     0    1\n","Clutch              0     0    1\n","Collision           0     0    4\n","Did not prequalify  0   330    0\n","Did not qualify     0  1022    0\n","Driver unwell       0     0    1\n","Driveshaft          0     0    1\n","ERS                 0     0    1\n","Electrical          0     0    2\n","Engine              0     0   19\n","Excluded            8     0    0\n","Exhaust             0     0    1\n","Fatal 