ws with laps > 0, podium rows\")\n","print(letters.groupby(\"positionText\").agg(rows=(\"grid\", \"size\"),\n","                                          grid_above_0=(\"grid\", lambda g: (g > 0).sum()),\n","                                          laps_above_0=(\"laps\", lambda l: (l > 0).sum()),\n","                                          podiums=(\"positionOrder\", lambda p: (p <= 3).sum())))\n","\n","display(letters[letters[\"positionText\"] == \"E\"]\n","        .merge(clean[\"races\"][[\"raceId\", \"year\", \"name\"]], on=\"raceId\")\n","        [[\"year\", \"name\", \"driverId\", \"grid\", \"laps\", \"status\", \"positionOrder\"]])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e54076d3","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.029927,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.756654+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.726727+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **F means the driver did not get a grid slot:** all 1,364 F rows have a qualifying reason as status: `Did not qualify` (1,022), `Did not prequalify` (330), `107% Rule` (9) and `Injury` (3). In the other direction, every `Did not qualify` and `Did not prequalify` row is an F. The letter code and the status agree.\n","2) **W means the driver did not take the start, for many reasons:** only 226 of the 334 W rows have the status `Withdrew`; the rest give the cause, such as `Accident` (29), `Engine` (19), `Gearbox` (8) or an injury (14). 133 W rows have a grid position, so these drivers qualified and then could not start. On the other side, 20 rows with status `Withdrew` have a finishing position or `R`, so they did start and stopped during the race. The letter code, not the status text, tells us whether a driver started.\n","3) **E is mixed:** 8 of the 9 excluded rows completed no laps, so these drivers were excluded before the race. The 2015 Brazilian Grand Prix row is different: the driver started from grid 8, completed 70 laps, and was excluded after the race. That is a race we would have predicted, with a non-podium label, so it stays.\n","4) **None of these rows is a podium:** removing them takes away no positive labels, only rows whose outcome was settled before the start.\n","5) **A few rows do not fit:** 1 F row and 5 W rows show laps above 0. None of them is a podium, so we follow the letter code for them too.\n","\n","**Our rule:** remove every F and W row, and the E rows with no laps completed. `laps` is post-race information, but here it only decides which rows are in scope, never a feature, and only within the E rows, where the letter alone cannot tell us whether the driver started.\n","\n","**A limitation we accept:** 133 W drivers had a grid slot, so some withdrawals were only known very close to the start, possibly after our cutoff. They are a small group of certain non-podiums, so removing them barely changes the table.\n","\n","Next we apply all three changes and track the row count and podium share after each one."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":49,"id":"6a360b7f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.817406Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.816968Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.85907Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.857712Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.075633,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.861329+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.785696+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Indianapolis 500 races: 11 | seasons: 1950 - 1960\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>step</th>\n","      <th>rows</th>\n","      <th>podium %</th>\n","      <th>removed</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>after 1.7</td>\n","      <td>26580</td>\n","      <td>12.67</td>\n","      <td>NaN</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>without non-starters</td>\n","      <td>24874</td>\n","      <td>13.54</td>\n","      <td>1706.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2</th>\n","      <td>without Indianapolis 500</td>\n","      <td>24524</td>\n","      <td>13.61</td>\n","      <td>350.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                       step   rows  podium %  removed\n","0                 after 1.7  26580     12.67      NaN\n","1      without non-starters  24874     13.54   1706.0\n","2  without Indianapolis 500  24524     13.61    350.0"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Before: 1 'United States' circuits | 1 'Argentinian ' drivers\n","After:  12 'USA' circuits | 25 'Argentine' drivers | 42 nationality values\n"]}],"source":["def podium_share(table):\n","    return round(100 * (table[\"positionOrder\"] <= 3).mean(), 2)\n","\n","steps = [{\"step\": \"after 1.7\", \"rows\": len(clean[\"results\"]), \"podium %\": podium_share(clean[\"results\"])}]\n","\n","# 1) drivers who never started: F and W, and E rows with no laps\n","r = clean[\"results\"]\n","never_started = r[\"positionText\"].isin([\"F\", \"W\"]) | ((r[\"positionText\"] == \"E\") & (r[\"laps\"] == 0))\n","clean[\"results\"] = r[~never_started].copy()\n","steps.append({\"step\": \"without non-starters\", \"rows\": len(clean[\"results\"]), \"podium %\": podium_share(clean[\"results\"])})\n","\n","# 2) the Indianapolis 500, selected by race name (not by circuit)\n","indy = clean[\"races\"][clean[\"races\"][\"name\"] == \"Indianapolis 500\"]\n","print(\"Indianapolis 500 races:\", len(indy), \"| seasons:\", indy[\"year\"].min(), \"-\", indy[\"year\"].max())\n","clean[\"results\"] = clean[\"results\"][~clean[\"results\"][\"raceId\"].isin(indy[\"raceId\"])].copy()\n","steps.append({\"step\": \"without Indianapolis 500\", \"rows\": len(clean[\"results\"]), \"podium %\": podium_share(clean[\"results\"])})\n","\n","steps = pd.DataFrame(steps)\n","steps[\"removed\"] = -steps[\"rows\"].diff()\n","display(steps)\n","\n","# 3) one label per country and nationality\n","print(\"Before:\", (clean[\"circuits\"][\"country\"] == \"United States\").sum(), \"'United States' circuits |\",\n","      (clean[\"drivers\"][\"nationality\"] == \"Argentinian \").sum(), \"'Argentinian ' drivers\")\n","clean[\"circuits\"][\"country\"] = clean[\"circuits\"][\"country\"].replace({\"United States\": \"USA\"})\n","clean[\"drivers\"][\"nationality\"] = clean[\"drivers\"][\"nationality\"].replace({\"Argentinian \": \"Argentine\"})\n","print(\"After: \", (clean[\"circuits\"][\"country\"] == \"USA\").sum(), \"'USA' circuits |\",\n","      (clean[\"drivers\"][\"nationality\"] == \"Argentine\").sum(), \"'Argentine' drivers |\",\n","      clean[\"drivers\"][\"nationality\"].nunique(), \"nationality values\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c89da630","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.029445,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.920667+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.891222+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Non-starters were the largest group of rows outside our scope:** removing them took out 1,706 rows (1,364 F, 334 W and 8 E), 6.4% of the table. Since none of them was a podium, the podium share rose from 12.67% to 13.54%. The rows that are left are drivers who actually raced, which is what we predict.\n","2) **The Indianapolis 500 is gone:** 11 races from 1950 to 1960 and 350 rows, about 32 entrants per race, far more than a typical Grand Prix of that time. The podium share moved only slightly (13.54% → 13.61%). Its races stay in `races`, so the foreign keys from 1.6 still reconcile.\n","3) **Each country and nationality now has one label:** all 12 US circuits are labelled `USA`, and the 25 Argentine drivers share one label, leaving 42 nationality values instead of 43. Question 2 can now match drivers to circuits without missing anyone because of spelling.\n","\n","**What we do next:** Part B is complete. In Part C we repeat the EDA from Part A on the cleaned data to see what the cleaning changed."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"506a9579","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.029,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.978524+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:27.949524+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","## Part C — EDA after cleaning\n","\n","## 1.9 What did the cleaning change?\n","\n","The brief asks for EDA both before and after cleaning, to show the impact of the cleaning. We repeat three views from Part A on the cleaned data and put them next to the raw versions:\n","\n","1) **Missing values:** the audit from 1.2, run on `clean`, compared column by column with the raw audit.\n","2) **Rows removed:** how many rows each cleaning step took out of `results`.\n","3) **The season views from 1.3:** entrants per race, podium share and grid = 0, before and after."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":50,"id":"9a9ad510","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.045359Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.044832Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.341947Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.340843Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.333374,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.344034+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.01066+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Placeholders left in clean: 0\n","Columns whose missing share changed: 7 of 120\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr t