t had in 1.2, including `qualifying`, whose coverage gaps are a property of the data, not of our cleaning.\n","3) **Every change is a drop:** the removed rows were mostly drivers who never raced, so they had no finishing position, race time or fastest lap. `position` fell from 40.9% to 36.8% missing, and the time and fastest-lap columns by 2–3 points each.\n","4) **What is still missing does not affect us:** `position` is still missing for 36.8% of rows, because retired drivers are not classified, which is why our target uses the always-filled `positionOrder`. The time and fastest-lap columns are post-race and are never features."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"45ad4a17","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.030309,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.466664+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.436355+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Where did the rows go?** Each cleaning step that removed rows from `results`, and how many it removed."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":51,"id":"bb668915","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.528052Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.52753Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.692823Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.691805Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.1986,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.695103+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.496503+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x300 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["results: raw 26759 | clean 24524 | kept 91.6%\n"]}],"source":["removed = pd.Series({\"shared drives (1.7)\": len(raw[\"results\"]) - steps.loc[0, \"rows\"],\n","                     \"non-starters (1.8)\": steps.loc[1, \"removed\"],\n","                     \"Indianapolis 500 (1.8)\": steps.loc[2, \"removed\"]})\n","\n","ax = removed.plot(kind=\"barh\", figsize=(8, 3))\n","ax.invert_yaxis()\n","for i, v in enumerate(removed):\n","    ax.text(v, i, f\" {int(v):,}\", va=\"center\")\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"rows removed from results\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Rows removed by each cleaning step\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"results: raw\", len(raw[\"results\"]), \"| clean\", len(clean[\"results\"]),\n","      f\"| kept {100 * len(clean['results']) / len(raw['results']):.1f}%\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"31155a25","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.031272,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.757568+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.726296+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Non-starters were by far the largest removal:** 1,706 rows, against 350 for the Indianapolis 500 and 179 for shared drives (123 repeated drivers and the 56 rows of the 28 cars credited to two drivers).\n","2) **Most of the table is kept:** 24,524 of 26,759 rows (91.6%) remain. Each removal has a documented reason: a driver who never started (1.8), a race outside the scope of the question (1.8), or a second row for the same driver in the same race (1.7)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"092a9f7c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.031353,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.819198+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.787845+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Did the season picture change?** We redraw the views from 1.3 on the cleaned `results`: entrants per race, podium share, and the share of rows with grid = 0."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":52,"id":"41882096","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.882077Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.881676Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.472331Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.471405Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.62729,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.476828+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:28.849538+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1800x400 with 3 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows with grid = 0 after cleaning: 80 of 24524 | podiums among them: 0 | seasons: 1981 - 2024\n"]}],"source":["res_clean = clean[\"results\"].merge(clean[\"races\"][[\"raceId\", \"year\"]], on=\"raceId\", how=\"left\")\n","res_clean[\"podium\"] = res_clean[\"positionOrder\"] <= 3\n","\n","per_season_clean = res_clean.groupby(\"year\").agg(races=(\"raceId\", \"nunique\"),\n","                                                 rows=(\"raceId\", \"size\"),\n","                                                 podium_rows=(\"podium\", \"sum\"))\n","per_season_clean[\"entrants_per_race\"] = per_season_clean[\"rows\"] / per_season_clean[\"races\"]\n","per_season_clean[\"podium_share\"] = 100 * per_season_clean[\"podium_rows\"] / per_season_clean[\"rows\"]\n","grid_zero_clean = 100 * res_clean.groupby(\"year\")[\"grid\"].apply(lambda g: (g == 0).mean())\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(18, 4))\n","per_season[\"entrants_per_race\"].plot(ax=axes[0], label=\"raw\")\n","per_season_clean[\"entrants_per_race\"].plot(ax=axes[0], label=\"clean\")\n","axes[0].axhline(20, linestyle=\"--\", color=\"grey\")\n","axes[0].set_title(\"Average entrants per race\")\n","axes[0].set_ylabel(\"entrants\")\n","\n","per_season[\"podium_share\"].plot(ax=axes[1], label=\"raw\")\n","per_season_clean[\"podium_share\"].plot(ax=axes[1], label=\"clean\")\n","axes[1].axhline(15, linestyle=\"--\", color=\"grey\")\n","axes[1].set_title(\"Share of result rows that are podiums\")\n","axes[1].set_ylabel(\"%\")\n","\n","grid_zero_share.sum(axis=1).plot(ax=axes[2], label=\"raw\")\n","grid_zero_clean.plot(ax=axes[2], label=\"clean\")\n","axes[2].set_title(\"Share of rows with grid = 0\")\n","axes[2].set_ylabel(\"% of result rows\")\n","\n","for ax in axes:\n","    ax.legend()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","grid0 = res_clean[res_clean[\"grid\"] == 0]\n","print(\"Rows with grid = 0 after cleaning:\", len(grid0), \"of\", len(res_clean),\n","      \"| podiums among them:\", grid0[\"podium\"].sum(),\n","      \"| seasons:\", grid0[\"year\"].min(), \"-\", grid0[\"year\"].max())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2ba9cebb","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.035122,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.546423+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.511301+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The late-1980s peak in field size came from non-starters:** in the raw data the average number of entrants per race climbs to almost 39 around 1989. After cleaning it stays around 25–26, because most of those entrants failed to (pre-)qualify. From the late 1990s the two lines are almost identical, since modern seasons have hardly any non-starters.\n","2) **The podium share is much more stable, but not constant:** the raw dip to about 8% around 1989 is gone. After cleaning the share stays between about 11.5% and 19%, and from around 2010 it sits close to the expected 15% (3 of 20). The remaining variation follows real field sizes: more starters means a lower share. The base rate of a podium therefore depends on the era, which matters for the data split and is a limitation we report.\n","3) **Almost all grid = 0 rows were non-starters:** the raw peaks above 20% in the early 1960s and above 30% around 1989 disappear completely. Only 80 of 24,524 rows still have grid 0, all from 1981–2024, mostly in the last few seasons, and none of them is a podium.\n","4) **The remaining grid 0 means a pit-lane start:** these drivers raced but did not start from a grid slot, which is how the F1 introduction describes grid 0. As a number, 0 would look better than pole position, so in Section 3 we must recode it as starting from the back rather than leave it as 0.\n","\n","**Summary of Part C:** the cleaning removed rows that were never predictions (non-starters, the Indianapolis 500 and second rows from shared drives). What remains is one row per driver who actually raced, with a podium share that is much closer to what each era's field size implies."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1ac52b79","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.032411,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.614615+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.582204+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","# 2. Data-Engineering Questions\n","\n","The brief asks three questions that can only be answered by combining several tables. For each one we give the answer, a plot, and a short note on grain, missingness and, where relevant, the pre-race cutoff.\n","\n","All three start from the cleaned `results` from Part B: one row per driver who raced in a race. These are descriptions of past races, not features, so they may use post-race columns such as the finishing position or the status. The pre-race restriction applies to the features we build in Section 3."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"54c1b616","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.032615,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.679593+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.646978+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Q1 · Front-row conversion by circuit, before and after 2014\n","\n","**Question:** which circuits convert a front-row start into a podium most often, and does that ranking change after the 2014 hybrid era? The brief asks us to distinguish qualifying position from grid.\n","\n","**Tables:** `results` → `races` (season and circuit) → `circuits` (circuit name), plus `qualifying` (qualifying position), joined on race and driver. The row count before and after the joins, printed below, confirms that they add no rows.\n","\n","**Our definitions**\n","\n","1) **Front-row start:** grid 1 or 2, where the car actually started; or qualifying position 1 or 2, where the driver qualified. The F1 introduction explains why the two can differ: penalties move drivers back, and in 2021–2022 the sprint set the grid on sprint weekends.\n","2) **Conversion rate:** the share of a circuit's front-row starters who finished on the podium.\n","3) **Eras:** before 2014 vs 2014 onward. The 2022–2024 seasons are counted in \"2014 onward\", because the question asks whether the ranking changed from 2014.\n","4) **Time windows:** grid is known for every season, so we compare 1950–2013 with 2014–2024. Qualifying is only complete from 2003 (plot 3 in 1.3), so for qualifying we compare 2003–2013 with 2014–2024.\n","5) **Minimum sample:** a circuit is ranked only if it has at least 10 front-row starts in each era, about five races. With fewer, a single result moves the rate by more than 10 points.\n","\n","First we build the table and check it."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":53,"id":"07c40a2b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.748553Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.748086Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.803329Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.801877Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.092846,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.805622+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.712776+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows before and after the joins: 24524 24524\n","\n","Front-row starters (grid 1 or 2) per race:\n","1      14\n","2    1098\n","4       1\n","Name: count, dtype: int64\n","Races with no front-row starter at all: 1\n","\n","Rows from 2003 without a qualifying position: 21 of 8910\n","started 1-2    False  True \n","qualified 1-2              \n","False           8022     36\n","True              37    815\n"]}],"source":["# cleaned results + season, circuit and qualifying position (also reused in Q2 and Q3)\n","base = (clean[\"results\"]\n","        .merge(clean[\"races\"][[\"raceId\", \"year\", \"circuitId\"]], on=\"raceId\", how=\"left\")\n","        .merge(clean[\"circuits\"][[\"circuitId\", \"name\", \"country\"]].rename(columns={\"name\": \"circuit\"}),\n","               on=\"circuitId\", how=\"left\")\n","        .merge(clean[\"qualifying\"][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"position\"]].rename(columns={\"position\": \"quali_pos\"}),\n","               on=[\"raceId\", \"driverId\"], how=\"left\"))\n","base[\"podium\"] = base[\"positionOrder\"] <= 3\n","base[\"era\"] = np.where(base[\"year\"] >= 2014, \"2014+\", \"before 2014\")\n","print(\"Rows before and after the joins:\", len(clean[\"results\"]), len(base))\n","\n","# does every race have exactly two front-row starters on the grid?\n","front_per_race = base[base[\"grid\"].isin([1, 2])].groupby(\"raceId\").size()\n","print(\"\\nFront-row starters (grid 1 or 2) per race:\")\n","print(front_per_race.value_counts().sort_index())\n","print(\"Races with no front-row starter at all:\", base[\"raceId\"].nunique() - len(front_per_race))\n","\n","# from 2003 qualifying is complete: how often do qualifying and grid disagree on the front row?\n","modern = base[base[\"year\"] >= 2003]\n","print(\"\\nRows from 2003 without a qualifying position:\", modern[\"quali_pos\"].isna().sum(), \"of\", len(modern))\n","print(pd.crosstab(modern[\"quali_pos\"].isin([1, 2]), modern[\"grid\"].isin([1, 2]),\n","                  rownames=[\"qualified 1-2\"], colnames=[\"started 1-2\"]))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1ffe03da","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.032467,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.869929+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.837462+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The joins kept every row:** 24,524 before and after, so adding season, circuit and qualifying position created no duplicates.\n","2) **Almost every race has exactly two front-row starters:** 1,098 of the 1,114 races. 14 have only one, one has none (the 2005 United States Grand Prix, where only 6 drivers remain after removing non-starters) and one has four (the 1952 Italian Grand Prix, where two drivers are recorded on grid 1 and two on grid 2). These 16 races are too few to change the rates noticeably.\n","3) **Qualifying is almost complete from 2003:** only 21 of 8,910 rows from 2003 have no qualifying position.\n","4) **Qualifying and grid usually agree on the front row, but not always:** of the 852 drivers who qualified 1st or 2nd since 2003, 37 did not start from the front row, and 36 drivers started on the front row without qualifying there. The F1 introduction gives the reasons: penalties, and the sprint setting the grid in 2021–2022. This is the difference the brief asks us to keep apart, so we compute the conversion both ways."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"ff44108e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.03237,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.93475+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.90238+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Conversion rate per circuit.** We compute the rate for each circuit and era, once with grid and once with qualifying position, keep the circuits with enough starts in both eras, and measure how much the ranking changed with a rank correlation between the two eras. 1 would mean the order of circuits stayed exactly the same, 0 that it is unrelated."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":54,"id":"e90798b7","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:30.000431Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.999962Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.200242Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.199261Z"},"papermill":{"duration":2.237237,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.203724+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:29.966487+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Grid 1-2 (1950-2013 vs 2014-2024) | circuits ranked: 16 | rank correlation between eras: -0.08\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n"