s=\"era\", values=\"podium\", aggfunc=[\"size\", \"mean\"])\n","    table.columns = [(\"starts \" if agg == \"size\" else \"rate \") + era for agg, era in table.columns]\n","    enough = (table[\"starts before 2014\"] >= MIN_STARTS) & (table[\"starts 2014+\"] >= MIN_STARTS)\n","    return table[enough].sort_values(\"rate 2014+\", ascending=False)\n","\n","views = {\"Grid 1-2 (1950-2013 vs 2014-2024)\": conversion(base, \"grid\"),\n","         \"Qualifying 1-2 (2003-2013 vs 2014-2024)\": conversion(modern, \"quali_pos\")}\n","\n","for title, t in views.items():\n","    print(title, \"| circuits ranked:\", len(t),\n","          \"| rank correlation between eras:\", round(t[\"rate before 2014\"].corr(t[\"rate 2014+\"], method=\"spearman\"), 2))\n","    display(t.round(2))\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 0.35 * max(len(t) for t in views.values()) + 2))\n","for ax, (title, t) in zip(axes, views.items()):\n","    t = t.sort_values(\"rate 2014+\")\n","    y = np.arange(len(t))\n","    ax.hlines(y, t[\"rate before 2014\"], t[\"rate 2014+\"], color=\"lightgrey\")\n","    ax.scatter(t[\"rate before 2014\"], y, label=\"before 2014\")\n","    ax.scatter(t[\"rate 2014+\"], y, label=\"2014+\")\n","    ax.set_yticks(y)\n","    ax.set_yticklabels(t.index)\n","    ax.set_xlabel(\"share of front-row starters finishing on the podium\")\n","    ax.set_title(title)\n","    ax.legend()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"90c782b4","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036112,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.277869+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.241757+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Front-row starts convert more often from 2014:** the rate rose at almost every ranked circuit. In the grid view it lies between 0.47 and 0.70 before 2014 and between 0.59 and 0.89 from 2014. Only Hungaroring fell (0.68 → 0.59), and Bahrain stayed the same (0.67).\n","2) **Using grid, the ranking changed completely:** the rank correlation between the eras is −0.08, so knowing a circuit's place before 2014 tells us nothing about its place after. Monaco went from one of the lowest rates (0.50) to the highest (0.89), and Hungaroring from one of the highest (0.68) to the lowest (0.59). But this view compares 2014–2024 with 64 very different seasons; the F1 introduction notes much lower reliability in the early decades, which lowers every pre-2014 rate regardless of the circuit.\n","3) **Using qualifying on comparable seasons, the ranking partly holds:** comparing 2003–2013 with 2014–2024, the rank correlation is 0.54. Suzuka and Spa are near the top in both eras, and Hungaroring stays near the bottom (0.59 in both). Yas Marina (0.60 → 0.82) and Monaco (0.68 → 0.89) rose the most, while Bahrain kept the same rate (0.67) and so fell from mid-table to second-last as the others rose.\n","4) **Grid and qualifying give different rankings at some circuits:** from 2014 the two views agree at most circuits (Monaco and Suzuka 0.89, Spa 0.82), but at Autódromo José Carlos Pace a grid front row converted 0.79 of the time and a qualifying front row only 0.68, moving it from 6th to 12th. Which definition we use matters.\n","\n","**Answer to Q1:** since 2014, Circuit de Monaco and Suzuka convert a front-row start into a podium most often (89% of front-row starters, by both grid and qualifying), followed by Yas Marina, Spa-Francorchamps and Barcelona-Catalunya (82–86%). The ranking did change after 2014. Measured by grid over the full history, the old and new rankings are unrelated (rank correlation −0.08). Measured by qualifying on comparable seasons (2003–2013 vs 2014–2024), it changed moderately (0.54): Monaco rose from mid-table to the top, while Hungaroring stayed at the bottom.\n","\n","**Grain, missingness and cutoff**\n","- **Grain:** one row per driver per race (cleaned in 1.7–1.8). A circuit's rate is podiums ÷ front-row starts at that circuit. Circuits are grouped by `circuitId`, so layout changes over the decades are not visible.\n","- **Missingness:** grid is complete. Qualifying does not exist before 1994 and is incomplete in 1996–2002, so the qualifying view starts in 2003, where only 21 of 8,910 rows lack a qualifying position. Red Bull Ring and Autódromo Hermanos Rodríguez drop out of that view because they have fewer than 10 front-row starts in 2003–2013.\n","- **Sample size:** each circuit has only 10–26 front-row starts per era (more before 2014 in the grid view), so one podium moves a rate by 4–10 points. Small differences, such as Silverstone's 0.77 vs 0.75, are within that noise.\n","- **Pre-race cutoff:** grid and qualifying position are both known before the race, and the podium is the outcome we describe. A circuit's rate also reflects which teams were strong in those seasons, not only the track itself."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5eb88311","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036637,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.350812+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.314175+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Q2 · Do drivers podium more often at home?\n","\n","**Question:** do drivers podium more often at a circuit in their home country than elsewhere, after controlling for starting position? A simple home-vs-away comparison is not enough, because home drivers might simply start further forward.\n","\n","**Tables:** `results` → `drivers` (nationality) → `races` → `circuits` (country). `base` from Q1 already holds the circuit's country.\n","\n","**Our decisions**\n","\n","1) **Nationality → country:** nationalities are adjectives (`British`) and circuit countries are names (`UK`), so we write the mapping out explicitly. The code stops if any nationality is missing from it.\n","2) **Dual nationalities** (`American-Italian`, `Argentine-Italian`): a race counts as home if it is held in either country.\n","3) **East German drivers:** Germany counts as home. As noted in 1.1, there are only three of them, so this choice cannot change the answer.\n","4) **Nationalities whose country never hosted a race:** these drivers can never race at home, so all their rows count as away.\n","5) **Controlling for starting position:** we split the grid into buckets (1, 2–3, 4–6, 7–10, 11+, and pit lane for grid 0) and compare home and away only within the same bucket."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":55,"id":"c6d438fe","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.433256Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.432707Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.571427Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.570027Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.183576,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.573732+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.390156+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows before and after the join: 24524 24524\n","Home rows: 1916 of 24524 (7.8%)\n","Nationalities that can never race at home: ['Chilean', 'Colombian', 'Czech', 'Danish', 'Finnish', 'Indonesian', 'Irish', 'Liechtensteiner', 'New Zealander', 'Polish', 'Rhodesian', 'Thai', 'Uruguayan', 'Venezuelan']\n","\n","Without controlling for grid:\n","        rows  podium_rate  median_grid\n","home                                  \n","False  22608        0.138         11.0\n","True    1916        0.117         13.0\n"]}],"source":["# nationality -> the country (or countries) that counts as home, written as in circuits.country\n","HOME_COUNTRIES = {\n","    \"American\": [\"USA\"], \"American-Italian\": [\"USA\", \"Italy\"], \"Argentine\": [\"Argentina\"],\n","    \"Argentine-Italian\": [\"Argentina\", \"Italy\"], \"Australian\": [\"Australia\"], \"Austrian\": [\"Austria\"],\n","    \"Belgian\": [\"Belgium\"], \"Brazilian\": [\"Brazil\"], \"British\": [\"UK\"], \"Canadian\": [\"Canada\"],\n","    \"Chilean\": [\"Chile\"], \"Chinese\": [\"China\"], \"Colombian\": [\"Colombia\"], \"Czech\": [\"Czech Republic\"],\n","    \"Danish\": [\"Denmark\"], \"Dutch\": [\"Netherlands\"], \"East German\": [\"Germany\"], \"Finnish\": [\"Finland\"],\n","    \"French\": [\"France\"], \"German\": [\"Germany\"], \"Hong Kong\": [\"Hong Kong\"], \"Hungarian\": [\"Hungary\"],\n","    \"Indian\": [\"India\"], \"Indonesian\": [\"Indonesia\"], \"Irish\": [\"Ireland\"], \"Italian\": [\"Italy\"],\n","    \"Japanese\": [\"Japan\"], \"Liechtensteiner\": [\"Liechtenstein\"], \"Malaysian\": [\"Malaysia\"],\n","    \"Mexican\": [\"Mexico\"], \"Monegasque\": [\"Monaco\"], \"New Zealander\": [\"New Zealand\"],\n","    \"Polish\": [\"Poland\"], \"Portuguese\": [\"Portugal\"], \"Rhodesian\": [\"Rhodesia\"], \"Russian\": [\"Russia\"],\n","    \"South African\": [\"South Africa\"], \"Spanish\": [\"Spain\"], \"Swedish\": [\"Sweden\"],\n","    \"Swiss\": [\"Switzerland\"], \"Thai\": [\"Thailand\"], \"Uruguayan\": [\"Uruguay\"], \"Venezuelan\": [\"Venezuela\"]}\n","\n","missing = set(clean[\"drivers\"][\"nationality\"]) - set(HOME_COUNTRIES)\n","assert not missing, f\"nationalities without a mapping: {missing}\"\n","\n","q2 = base.merge(clean[\"drivers\"][[\"driverId\", \"nationality\"]], on=\"driverId\", how=\"left\")\n","q2[\"home\"] = [country in HOME_COUNTRIES[nat] for nat, country in zip(q2[\"nationality\"], q2[\"country\"])]\n","print(\"Rows before and after the join:\", len(base), len(q2))\n","print(\"Home rows:\", q2[\"home\"].sum(), \"of\", len(q2), f\"({100 * q2['home'].mean():.1f}%)\")\n","\n","circuit_countries = set(clean[\"circuits\"][\"country\"])\n","never_home = sorted(n for n, cs in HOME_COUNTRIES.items()\n","                    if n in set(q2[\"nationality\"]) and not set(cs) & circuit_countries)\n","print(\"Nationalities that can never race at home:\", never_home)\n","\n","print(\"\\nWithout controlling for grid:\")\n","print(q2.groupby(\"home\").agg(rows=(\"podium\", \"size\"), podium_rate=(\"podium\", \"mean\"),\n","                             median_grid=(\"grid\", \"median\")).round(3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b25d76cb","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.039391,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.651237+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.611846+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The mapping covers every driver:** the code found no nationality without a home country, and the join kept all 24,524 rows.\n","2) **Home races are a small share:** 1,916 rows (7.8%) are a driver racing in their home country.\n","3) **14 nationalities can never race at home:** their countries never hosted a race in our data (for example `Finnish`, `New Zealander` or `Danish`). All their rows count as away.\n","4) **Without any control, home drivers do worse, not better:** 11.7% of home rows are podiums against 13.8% away. But home drivers also start further back (median grid 13 against 11). The F1 introduction mentions one possible reason: one-off local drivers who entered only their home race. So the raw comparison mixes the home effect with starting position, which is exactly why the question asks us to control for it."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1cb2e1d3","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.038619,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.726578+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.687959+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Controlling for starting position.** We put every row in a grid bucket and compare the podium rate of home and away drivers within each bucket. The error bars show a 95% interval for each rate. Where the home and away intervals overlap a lot, the data cannot tell the two apart."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":56,"id":"baa33cc3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.805196Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.804739Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.083446Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.082406Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.319849,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.085869+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:32.76602+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>rows away</th>\n","      <th>rows home</th>\n","      <th>rate away</th>\n","      <th>rate home</th>\n","      <th>difference</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>grid_bucket</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>pit lane</th>\n","      <td>77</td>\n","      <td>3</td>\n","      <td>0.000</td>\n","      <td>0.000</td>\n","      <td>0.000</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>1024</td>\n","      <td>80</td>\n","      <td>0.650</td>\n","      <td>0.612</td>\n","      <td>-0.038</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2-3</th>\n","      <td>2071</td>\n","      <td>148</td>\n","      <td>0.510</td>\n","      <td>0.534</td>\n","      <td>0.023</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>4-6</th>\n","      <td>3106</td>\n","      <td>224</td>\n","      <td>0.260</td>\n","      <td>0.268</td>\n","      <td>0.008</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>7-10</th>\n","      <td>4087</td>\n","      <td>330</td>\n","      <td>0.093</td>\n","      <td>0.073</td>\n","      <td>-0.020</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>11+</th>\n","      <td>12243</td>\n","      <td>1131</td>\n","      <td>0.017</td>\n","      <td>0.011</td>\n","      <td>-0.006</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["             rows away  rows home  rate away  rate home  difference\n","grid_bucket                                                        \n","pit lane            77          3      0.000      0.000       0.000\n","1                 1024         80      0.650      0.612      -0.038\n","2-3               2071        148      0.510      0.534       0.023\n","4-6               3106        224      0.260      0.268       0.008\n","7-10              4087        330      0.093      0.073      -0.020\n","11+              12243       1131      0.017      0.011      -0.006"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["q2[\"grid_bucket\"] = pd.cut(q2[\"grid\"], bins=[-0.5, 0.5, 1.5, 3.5, 6.5, 10.5, np.inf],\n","                           labels=[\"pit lane\", \"1\", \"2-3\", \"4-6\", \"7-10\", \"11+\"])\n","\n","by_bucket = q2.groupby([\"grid_bucket\", \"home\"], observed=True)[\"podium\"].agg([\"size\", \"mean\"]).unstack(\"home\")\n","by_bucket.columns = [f\"{'rows' if s == 'size' else 'rate'} {'home' if h else 'away'}\" for s, h in by_bucket.columns]\n","by_bucket[\"difference\"] = by_bucket[\"rate home\"] - by_bucket[\"rate away\"]\n","display(by_bucket.round(3))\n","\n","x = np.arange(len(by_bucket))\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 4))\n","for offset, side in [(-0.2, \"away\"), (0.2, \"home\")]:\n","    rate, n = by_bucket[f\"rate {side}\"], by_bucket[f\"rows {side}\"]\n","    ax.bar(x + offset, rate, width=0.4, label=side,\n","           yerr=1.96 * np.sqrt(rate * (1 - rate) / n), capsize=3)\n","    for xi, r, ni in zip(x + offset, rate, n):\n","        ax.text(xi, r + 0.03, f\"n={int(ni)}\", ha=\"center\", fontsize=8)\n","ax.set_xticks(x)\n","ax.set_xticklabels(by_bucket.index)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"starting position (grid bucket)\")\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"podium rate\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Podium rate at home vs away, within the same grid bucket\")\n","ax.legend()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"dd41584b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.037131,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.160357+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.123226+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Within the same grid bucket, home and away are almost identical:** the difference in podium rate is between −3.8 and +2.3 percentage points, and it changes sign. Home drivers do slightly better from 2nd–3rd (0.534 vs 0.510) and 4th–6th (0.268 vs 0.260), and slightly worse from pole (0.612 vs 0.650), 7th–10th (0.073 vs 0.093) and 11th or lower (0.011 vs 0.017).\n","2) **None of these differences is clearly larger than the uncertainty:** in every bucket the 95% intervals of the home and away rates overlap. Home samples are small (80 home pole starts against 1,024 away), so their intervals are wide. The closest case is 11th or lower (1.1% vs 1.7%), where the home interval only just reaches the away interval.\n","3) **Starting position decides almost everything:** the podium rate falls from about 0.6 from pole to about 0.5 from 2nd–3rd, 0.26 from 4th–6th, under 0.1 from 7th–10th and under 0.02 from 11th or lower. No pit-lane starter reached the podium, home or away. This supports `grid` as a main feature in Section 3.\n","\n","**Answer to Q2:** no. Without any control, home drivers podium less often than away drivers (11.7% vs 13.8%), because they tend to start further back. Once we compare drivers who started from similar grid positions, the home and away podium rates are nearly the same in every bucket. The differences are small, go in both directions, and fall within the uncertainty of the data. We find no evidence of a home advantage.\n","\n","**Grain, missingness and cutoff**\n","- **Grain:** one row per driver per race (cleaned). A row is \"home\" if the circuit's country is the driver's country, or either country for dual nationalities.\n","- **Missingness:** nationality, circuit country and grid are complete, so no row was left out. 14 nationalities never have a home race, which is a property of the calendar, not missing data.\n","- **Choices that could matter:** East German drivers counted as at home in Germany (3 drivers); dual nationalities counted as at home in either country; the Indianapolis 500 excluded in 1.8, since it would add many home rows for American drivers who rarely raced elsewhere.\n","- **What we did not control for:** grid buckets control for starting position only. Team strength and era are not held constant.\n","- **Pre-race cutoff:** nationality, circuit and grid are all known before the race; the podium is the outcome we describe."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"380204e2","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.038567,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.237545+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.198978+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Q3 · Mechanical retirements by constructor, 2014–2021 vs 2022–2024\n","\n","**Question:** which constructors have the highest mechanical-retirement rate in 2014–2021 vs 2022–2024? The brief defines a mechanical retirement as a race start that ended early because a component of the car failed, excluding failures caused by a crash, by the driver, or by a regulation decision.\n","\n","**Tables:** `results` → `status` (why the race ended) → `races` (season) → `constructors` (team name). `base` from Q1 already holds the season.\n","\n","**Our decisions**\n","\n","1) **Race starts only:** the denominator is every driver who started, which after 1.8 is every row of the cleaned `results`.\n","2) **Rate** = mechanical retirements ÷ race starts, per constructor and period.\n","3) **Constructors are grouped by `constructorId`:** as the F1 introduction says, a renamed team gets a new ID, so its history restarts under the new name.\n","4) **The status mapping:** `status` has no mechanical/non-mechanical label, so we build one. First we list every reason a race ended in 2014–2024 that was not a finish, so the mapping covers every value that actually occurs."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":57,"id":"674bcbc6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.312998Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.312547Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.34001Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.338135Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.068318,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.342549+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.274231+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows before and after the joins: 4598 4598\n","Race starts 2014-2024: 4598 | finished or lapped: 3825 | ended early: 773\n","\n","Reasons for ending early, 2014-2024:\n","status\n","Collision           150\n","Accident             85\n","Engine               79\n","Collision damage     59\n","Retired              49\n","Brakes               48\n","Gearbox              40\n","Power Unit           39\n","Suspension           25\n","Electrical           14\n","Hydraulics           14\n","Power loss           12\n","Wheel                11\n","Spun off             11\n","Disqualified         11\n","Oil leak             10\n","Overheating           8\n","Water pressure        7\n","Puncture              7\n","Mechanical            7\n","Turbo                 6\n","Battery               5\n","Fuel pressure         5\n","ERS                   4\n","Undertray             4\n","Tyre                  4\n","Exhaust               4\n","Electronics           4\n","Water leak            4\n","Rear wing             3\n","Wheel nut             3\n","Transmission          3\n","Withdrew              3\n","Radiator              3\n","Front wing            3\n","Technical             2\n","Damage                2\n","Clutch                2\n","Oil pressure          2\n","Throttle              2\n","Steering              2\n","Illness               2\n","Vibrations            2\n","Drivetrain            1\n","Driveshaft            1\n","Excluded              1\n","Brake duct            1\n","Spark plugs           1\n","Debris                1\n","Out of fuel           1\n","Seat                  1\n","Cooling system        1\n","Water pump            1\n","Fuel leak             1\n","Fuel pump             1\n","Differential          1\n"]}],"source":["q3 = (base[base[\"year\"] >= 2014]\n","      .merge(clean[\"status\"], on=\"statusId\", how=\"left\")\n","      .merge(clean[\"constructors\"][[\"constructorId\", \"name\"]].rename(columns={\"name\": \"constructor\"}),\n","             on=\"constructorId\", how=\"left\"))\n","q3[\"period\"] = np.where(q3[\"year\"] <= 2021, \"2014-2021\", \"2022-2024\")\n","print(\"Rows before and after the joins:\", (base[\"year\"] >= 2014).sum(), len(q3))\n","\n","finished = (q3[\"status\"] == \"Finished\") | q3[\"status\"].str.match(r\"^\\+\\d+ Laps?$\")\n","print(\"Race starts 2014-2024:\", len(q3), \"| finished or lapped:\", finished.sum(),\n","      \"| ended early:\", (~finished).sum())\n","print(\"\\nReasons for ending early, 2014-2024:\")\n","print(q3.loc[~finished, \"status\"].value_counts().to_string())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7f5d6601","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036569,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.417115+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.380546+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The joins kept every row:** 4,598 race starts from 2014 to 2024, of which 3,825 (83%) finished or were lapped and 773 ended early.\n","2) **Crashes are the most common reason, but car failures are many and varied:** `Collision` (150) and `Accident` (85) lead, but 56 different reasons occur, and most of them name a part of the car (`Engine` 79, `Brakes` 48, `Gearbox` 40, `Power Unit` 39 and many smaller ones).\n","3) **Some reasons do not fit the brief's definition cleanly:** some name damage rather than a failure (`Collision damage`, `Damage`, `Puncture`, `Tyre`, `Debris`), some could be either (`Wheel`, `Front wing`, `Rear wing`), and `Retired` (49) gives no reason at all.\n","\n","**Our mapping**\n","\n","Following the brief, a retirement is mechanical if a component of the car failed, and not mechanical if a crash, the driver or a regulation decision ended the race.\n","\n","| Group | Reasons | Why |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **Mechanical** | every reason that names a part or system of the car: `Engine`, `Power Unit`, `Gearbox`, `Brakes`, `Suspension`, `Hydraulics`, `Electrical`, … (full list in the code) | a component failed |\n","| **Mechanical, but debatable** | `Wheel`, `Wheel nut`, `Front wing`, `Rear wing`, `Vibrations` | a part of the car failed or came loose; the data does not say whether contact caused it, and the brief only excludes crashes, the driver and regulations |\n","| **Not mechanical: crash** | `Collision`, `Accident`, `Collision damage`, `Damage`, `Spun off` | caused by a crash or the driver |\n","| **Not mechanical: tyre damage** | `Puncture`, `Tyre`, `Debris` | usually caused by debris or contact, not by a failing part |\n","| **Not mechanical: other** | `Disqualified`, `Excluded` (regulation), `Illness`, `Withdrew` (driver), `Out of fuel` (no part failed) | not a component failure |\n","| **Unknown** | `Retired` | no reason recorded; not counted as mechanical |\n","\n","The debatable mechanical reasons cover 22 retirements and the tyre-damage reasons 12, against 387 mechanical retirements in total, so these choices can only move a team's rate slightly. `Retired` (49) is larger, and we report it as a limitation."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":58,"id":"71a99e1d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.492574Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.492101Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.533846Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.532319Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.082603,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.53625+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.453647+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["period          2014-2021  2022-2024   All\n","outcome                                   \n","finished             2660       1165  3825\n","mechanical            307         80   387\n","not mechanical        242         95   337\n","unknown                37         12    49\n","All                  3246       1352  4598\n"]}],"source":["MECHANICAL = [\"Engine\", \"Power Unit\", \"Gearbox\", \"Brakes\", \"Suspension\", \"Electrical\", \"Hydraulics\",\n","              \"Power loss\", \"Oil leak\", \"Overheating\", \"Water pressure\", \"Mechanical\", \"Turbo\", \"Battery\",\n","              \"Fuel pressure\", \"ERS\", \"Undertray\", \"Exhaust\", \"Electronics\", \"Water leak\", \"Transmission\",\n","              \"Radiator\", \"Technical\", \"Clutch\", \"Oil pressure\", \"Throttle\", \"Steering\", \"Drivetrain\",\n","              \"Driveshaft\", \"Brake duct\", \"Spark plugs\", \"Seat\", \"Cooling system\", \"Water pump\",\n","              \"Fuel leak\", \"Fuel pump\", \"Differential\",\n","              \"Wheel\", \"Wheel nut\", \"Front wing\", \"Rear wing\", \"Vibrations\"]          # debatable\n","NOT_MECHANICAL = [\"Collision\", \"Accident\", \"Collision damage\", \"Damage\", \"Spun off\",  # crash / driver\n","                  \"Puncture\", \"Tyre\", \"Debris\",                                      # tyre damage\n","                  \"Disqualified\", \"Excluded\", \"Illness\", \"Withdrew\", \"Out of fuel\"]  # other\n","UNKNOWN = [\"Retired\"]\n","\n","# every reason for ending early must be in exactly one group\n","early = set(q3.loc[~finished, \"status\"])\n","groups = [set(MECHANICAL), set(NOT_MECHANICAL), set(UNKNOWN)]\n","assert early == set().union(*groups), f\"unmapped: {early - set().union(*groups)}\"\n","assert sum(len(g) for g in groups) == len(set().union(*groups)), \"a reason is in two groups\"\n","\n","q3[\"outcome\"] = np.select([finished, q3[\"status\"].isin(MECHANICAL), q3[\"status\"].isin(NOT_MECHANICAL)],\n","                          [\"finished\", \"mechanical\", \"not mechanical\"], default=\"unknown\")\n","print(pd.crosstab(q3[\"outcome\"], q3[\"period\"], margins=True))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e441610a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.038684,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.613455+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.574771+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Mechanical-retirement rate per constructor.** For each constructor and period: mechanical retirements ÷ race starts. A constructor is ranked only if it has at least 20 starts in that period (10 race weekends with two cars), so a team that raced only briefly cannot top the ranking by chance."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1921c233","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.037156,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.688002+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.650846+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The mapping covers every reason exactly once:** both checks passed, and the totals match the list above: 387 mechanical, 337 not mechanical, 49 unknown.\n","2) **Mechanical failures became rarer:** 307 of 3,246 starts in 2014–2021 (9.5%) against 80 of 1,352 in 2022–2024 (5.9%). Crashes and other non-mechanical endings stayed more stable (7.5% and 7.0%).\n","3) **Unknown reasons are a small share:** 37 starts in 2014–2021 and 12 in 2022–2024 ended with `Retired` and no cause. Even if all of them were mechanical, the overall rates would rise by only about 1 percentage point."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":59,"id":"1589b596","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.766436Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:33.765414Z","iopub.status.idle"