6           5  0.037\n","23          Sauber      48           1  0.021"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x600 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["MIN_STARTS_Q3 = 20\n","\n","q3[\"mechanical\"] = q3[\"outcome\"] == \"mechanical\"\n","rates = (q3.groupby([\"period\", \"constructorId\", \"constructor\"])\n","           .agg(starts=(\"mechanical\", \"size\"), mechanical=(\"mechanical\", \"sum\"), rate=(\"mechanical\", \"mean\"))\n","           .reset_index())\n","print(\"Constructors below\", MIN_STARTS_Q3, \"starts (not ranked):\",\n","      rates.loc[rates[\"starts\"] < MIN_STARTS_Q3, [\"period\", \"constructor\", \"starts\"]].values.tolist())\n","rates = rates[rates[\"starts\"] >= MIN_STARTS_Q3]\n","\n","for period, t in rates.groupby(\"period\"):\n","    print(f\"\\n{period}: mechanical rate over all starts {q3.loc[q3['period'] == period, 'mechanical'].mean():.3f}\")\n","    display(t.sort_values(\"rate\", ascending=False)[[\"constructor\", \"starts\", \"mechanical\", \"rate\"]].round(3))\n","\n","periods = [\"2014-2021\", \"2022-2024\"]\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6), sharex=True)\n","for ax, period in zip(axes, periods):\n","    t = rates[rates[\"period\"] == period].sort_values(\"rate\")\n","    ax.barh(t[\"constructor\"], t[\"rate\"])\n","    for y, (r, n) in enumerate(zip(t[\"rate\"], t[\"starts\"])):\n","        ax.text(r, y, f\" {r:.1%} (n={n})\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8)\n","    ax.set_title(f\"Mechanical-retirement rate, {period}\")\n","    ax.set_xlabel(\"mechanical retirements ÷ race starts\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8e0ef9c7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.03571,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.406556+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.370846+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **2014–2021, highest rates:** Caterham (21.2%), Lotus F1 (18.7%) and Toro Rosso (16.1%), followed by Renault (14.1%) and McLaren (13.6%). Caterham and Lotus F1 have few starts (33 and 75), so their rates are less certain. Among the constructors that raced through the whole period (over 300 starts), McLaren has the highest rate and Mercedes the lowest (4.1%).\n","2) **2022–2024, highest rates:** Alfa Romeo (12.5%), Alpine F1 Team (10.4%) and AlphaTauri (8.0%). The lowest are Sauber (2.1%, only 48 starts), and Red Bull and McLaren (3.7% each).\n","3) **The ranking changed:** McLaren went from among the least reliable to joint second-best (13.6% → 3.7%), and Red Bull from 10.7% to 3.7%. Mercedes was among the most reliable in both periods (4.1% and 4.4%).\n","4) **One team lineage stays near the top:** the F1 introduction names Toleman → Benetton → Renault → Lotus → Alpine as one team under changing names. Its recent names are all high: Lotus F1 (18.7%) and Renault (14.1%) in 2014–2021, and Alpine (10.4%) in 2022–2024. Because we group by `constructorId`, as the introduction advises, these appear as separate constructors.\n","5) **Differences of a point or two are noise:** with about 135 starts per team in 2022–2024, one extra failure moves a rate by about 0.7 points (2 points for teams with 48 starts). Ferrari, Aston Martin and Haas at 5.2% (7 failures each) cannot be told apart.\n","\n","**Answer to Q3:** in 2014–2021 the highest mechanical-retirement rates belong to Caterham (21.2%), Lotus F1 (18.7%) and Toro Rosso (16.1%). Among full-period teams, McLaren is the highest (13.6%). In 2022–2024 they belong to Alfa Romeo (12.5%), Alpine F1 Team (10.4%) and AlphaTauri (8.0%). Mechanical failures became less common overall (9.5% → 5.9% of starts), and the ranking changed: McLaren and Red Bull moved from the upper half to the most reliable teams, while Mercedes stayed reliable in both periods.\n","\n","**Grain, missingness and cutoff**\n","- **Grain:** one row per driver per race start (cleaned), aggregated per constructor (`constructorId`) and period. Each car counts separately, so a two-car team has about twice as many starts as races.\n","- **Missingness:** `status` is complete. 49 retirements have only `Retired` and no cause; we count them as unknown, which can lower a team's mechanical rate by at most a few failures.\n","- **Mapping choices:** 22 debatable failures (`Wheel`, `Wheel nut`, wings, `Vibrations`) are counted as mechanical and 12 tyre-damage endings (`Puncture`, `Tyre`, `Debris`) as not mechanical. The full mapping is in the code above.\n","- **Renamed teams:** teams that changed name appear separately, and some names cover only part of a period (for example Alpine F1 Team, 44 starts in 2014–2021).\n","- **Pre-race cutoff:** `status` is post-race. Q3 describes past races and uses it as the outcome, so this is not leakage. In Section 3 a team's reliability could only be used from earlier races."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"5138ba7d","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.035406,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.477724+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.442318+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","# 3. Feature Selection & Engineering\n","\n","In this section we turn the cleaned results into the modeling table: one row per driver per race, with only information that is known after qualifying and before the race starts. Every feature has to pass two tests:\n","\n","1) **Available at the cutoff:** it must be known after qualifying and before the race starts; anything later would be leakage.\n","2) **Linked to a podium:** our data must show that it relates to finishing on the podium.\n","\n","We first decide which seasons the model learns from, because the window decides which features are possible and how much of each one is missing (qualifying coverage changes over time, 1.3). Then we build the features one group at a time (grid, qualifying, standings and form), each with the evidence behind it, and finally split the data into training, validation and test seasons."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"93fcdb64","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.035743,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.549964+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.514221+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.1 Which seasons do we model?\n","\n","Plot 3 in 1.3 showed that qualifying data does not exist before 1994 and covers only part of the races in 1996–2002. The F1 introduction lists three ways to deal with this: impute qualifying, fall back to `grid`, or restrict the training window. Before choosing, we measure what each starting season would give us: how many rows, how many of them have a qualifying position, and the podium rate."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":60,"id":"3fa9f899","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.627983Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.626737Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.656024Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.655046Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.06912,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.658447+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.589327+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>seasons</th>\n","      <th>rows</th>\n","      <th>rows with qualifying (%)</th>\n","      <th>podium rate (%)</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>1950-2024</td>\n","      <td>24524</td>\n","      <td>42.5</td>\n","      <td>13.6</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>1994-2024</td>\n","      <td>12219</td>\n","      <td>85.3</td>\n","      <td>14.2</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2</th>\n","      <td>2003-2024</td>\n","      <td>8910</td>\n","      <td>99.8</td>\n","      <td>14.4</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["     seasons   rows  rows with qualifying (%)  podium rate (%)\n","0  1950-2024  24524                      42.5             13.6\n","1  1994-2024  12219                      85.3             14.2\n","2  2003-2024   8910                      99.8             14.4"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["rows = (clean[\"results\"][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"positionOrder\"]]\n","        .merge(clean[\"races\"][[\"raceId\", \"year\"]], on=\"raceId\", how=\"left\")\n","        .merge(clean[\"qualifying\"][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"position\"]], on=[\"raceId\", \"driverId\"], how=\"left\"))\n","\n","window = []\n","for start in [1950, 1994, 2003]:\n","    w = rows[rows[\"year\"] >= start]\n","    window.append({\"seasons\": f\"{start}-2024\", \"rows\": len(w),\n","                   \"rows with qualifying (%)\": round(100 * w[\"position\"].notna().mean(), 1),\n","                   \"podium rate (%)\": round(100 * (w[\"positionOrder\"] <= 3).mean(), 1)})\n","display(pd.DataFrame(window))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2a903737","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036608,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.731577+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.694969+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Qualifying coverage decides the window:** over all seasons only 42.5% of rows have a qualifying position, so a qualifying feature would have to be guessed for most of the table. From 1994 it is still missing for about one row in seven. From 2003 it is missing for only 21 of 8,910 rows (99.8% complete).\n","2) **Podiums are just as common in every window:** the podium rate is the number of podium rows divided by all rows. Since every race has three podium places, it equals three divided by the average number of starters per race. It is 13.6% for 1950–2024, 14.2% for 1994–2024 and 14.4% for 2003–2024 (1,284 podiums in 428 races with about 21 starters each), so keeping only 2003–2024 does not make podiums rarer or more common in our data.\n","3) **The split fits inside the window:** the F1 introduction gives the season boundaries train ≤ 2019, validation 2020–2021 and test ≥ 2022. A window starting in 2003 contains all three, each with complete qualifying data.\n","\n","**The three options from the F1 introduction**\n","\n","1) **Impute qualifying:** keep every season and fill in the missing qualifying positions with estimates. Rejected: for most of the history we would be inventing the very information we want the model to learn from.\n","2) **Fall back to grid:** use the starting position where qualifying is missing. `grid` is complete for every season and, as 1.1 showed, it is known before the race, so it will be one of our features anyway. Falling back can mean two things, and neither works well:\n","   - copying `grid` into the qualifying column for older races, which gives the model nothing it does not already get from `grid` itself, or\n","   - dropping qualifying and keeping every season, which loses what qualifying adds on top of the grid: in Q1, 37 drivers since 2003 qualified on the front row but did not start there.\n","3) **Restrict the training window:** keep only the seasons where qualifying is complete. **Chosen.**\n","\n","**Our decision:** the model learns from the 2003–2024 seasons. The cost is fewer rows (8,910 instead of 24,524), but the seasons we keep are also closer to the 2022–2024 test seasons in field size, reliability and rules.\n","\n","**What this does not change:** form and standings features look back at earlier races. A 2003 race may still use results from 2002, so these features are built from the full cleaned history and only the rows we predict are limited to 2003–2024."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"69164c92","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.037228,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.805098+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.76787+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.2 The base table\n","\n","We start from the cleaned `results` (one row per driver who started a race) and attach what every later step needs: the season, round and date of the race from `races`, and the driver's qualifying position from `qualifying`. The driver's team (`constructorId`) is taken from `results`, as decided in 1.1, since it records the team the driver actually raced for.\n","\n","We keep all cleaned seasons here, not only 2003–2024. Form and standings features look back at earlier races, so a 2003 race must be able to see what happened in 2002. The rows are sorted by race date, because 1.1 showed that IDs are not in time order and every \"earlier races\" feature depends on the correct order.\n","\n","`positionOrder` stays in the table only to define the target and to describe past races. It is never used as a feature for the race it belongs to."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":61,"id":"d3174f3a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.880541Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.88017Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.929248Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.928272Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.089137,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.931252+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.842115+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows before and after the joins: 24524 24524\n","Duplicated (raceId, driverId): 0\n","Races sharing a date with another race: 0\n","Seasons: 1950 - 2024 | rows from 2003: 8910\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>raceId</th>\n","      <th>driverId</th>\n","      <th>constructorId</th>\n","      <th>grid</th>\n","      <th>positionOrder</th>\n","      <th>year</th>\n","      <th>round</th>\n","      <th>date</th>\n","      <th>quali_pos</th>\n","      <th>podium</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>24519</th>\n","      <td>1144</td>\n","      <td>825</td>\n","      <td>210</td>\n","      <td>14</td>\n","      <td>16</td>\n","      <td>2024</td>\n","      <td>24</td>\n","      <td>2024-12-08</td>\n","      <td>15.0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>24520</th>\n","      <td>1144</td>\n","      <td>859</td>\n","      <td>215</td>\n","      <td>12</td>\n","      <td>17</td>\n","      <td>2024</td>\n","      <td>24</td>\n","      <td>2024-12-08</td>\n","      <td>12.0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>24521</th>\n","      <td>1144</td>\n","      <td>822</td>\n","      <td>15</td>\n","      <td>9</td>\n","      <td>18</td>\n","      <td>2024</td>\n","      <td>24</td>\n","      <td>2024-12-08</td>\n","      <td>9.0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>24522</th>\n","      <td>1144</td>\n","      <td>861</td>\n","      <td>3</td>\n","      <td>20</td>\n","      <td>19</td>\n","      <td>2024</td>\n","      <td>24</td>\n","      <td>2024-12-08</td>\n","      <td>19.0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>24523</th>\n","      <td>1144</td>\n","      <td>815</td>\n","      <td>9</td>\n","      <td>10</td>\n","      <td>20</td>\n","      <td>2024</td>\n","      <td>24</td>\n","      <td>2024-12-08</td>\n","      <td>10.0</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["       raceId  driverId  constructorId  grid  positionOrder  year  round  \\\n","24519    1144       825            210    14             16  2024     24   \n","24520    1144       859            215    12             17  2024     24   \n","24521    1144       822             15     9             18  2024     24   \n","24522    1144       861              3    20             19  2024     24   \n","24523    1144       815              9    10             20  2024     24   \n","\n","            date  quali_pos  podium  \n","24519 2024-12-08       15.0       0  \n","24520 2024-12-08       12.0       0  \n","24521 2024-12-08        9.0       0  \n","24522 2024-12-08       19.0       0  \n","24523 2024-12-08       10.0       0  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["history = (clean[\"results\"][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"constructorId\", \"grid\", \"positionOrder\"]]\n","           .merge(clean[\"races\"][[\"raceId\", \"year\", \"round\", \"date\"]], on=\"raceId\", how=\"left\")\n","           .merge(clean[\"qualifying\"][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"position\"]].rename(columns={\"position\": \"quali_pos\"}),\n","                  on=[\"raceId\", \"driverId\"], how=\"left\"))\n","history[\"podium\"] = (history[\"positionOrder\"] <= 3).astype(int)\n","history = history.sort_values([\"date\", \"raceId\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","print(\"Rows before and after the joins:\", len(clean[\"results\"]), len(history))\n","print(\"Duplicated (raceId, driverId):\", history.duplicated([\"raceId\", \"driverId\"]).sum())\n","print(\"Races sharing a date with another race:\", history.groupby(\"raceId\")[\"date\"].first().duplicated().sum())\n","print(\"Seasons:\", history[\"year\"].min(), \"-\", history[\"year\"].max(),\n","      \"| rows from 2003:\", (history[\"year\"] >= 2003).sum())\n","display(history.tail())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9a9cdafe","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.03764,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.00514+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:34.9675+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The joins kept every row:** 24,524 before and after, and no driver appears twice in a race, so the table still has the grain we fixed in 1.7.\n","2) **Time order is well defined:** no two races share a date, so sorting by `date` puts every race in a single, clear order. This is the order every \"earlier races\" feature in this section relies on.\n","3) **History and modeling rows:** the table covers 1950–2024. The 8,910 rows from 2003 onward form the modeling table, later split into training (2003–2019), validation (2020–2021) and test (2022–2024) seasons. The earlier rows are kept only as history for features that look back at past races."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"bdb4867e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.037111,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.079103+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.041992+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.3 Grid\n","\n","`grid` is the position a car actually starts from, after penalties, and 1.1 showed it is known before the race. It is complete, but it contains the value 0, which 1.3 and 1.9 showed now means a pit-lane start: after cleaning, only drivers who really raced from the pit lane are left with grid 0. As a number, 0 would look better than pole position, so we recode it as a start from the back of the field, using the number of starters in that race.\n","\n","To keep the validation and test seasons unseen, the evidence for every feature in this section comes only from the training seasons, 2003–2019."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":62,"id":"3e0821ef","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.154566Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.15425Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.166829Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.165833Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.053254,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.168877+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.115623+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Pit-lane starts (grid 0) from 2003: 73 | podiums among them: 0\n"]}],"source":["# grid 0 is a pit-lane start (1.3, 1.9): count it as starting from the back of the field\n","history[\"starters\"] = history.groupby(\"raceId\")[\"driverId\"].transform(\"size\")\n","history[\"grid_pos\"] = history[\"grid\"].where(history[\"grid\"] > 0, history[\"starters\"])\n","\n","model_rows = history[\"year\"] >= 2003\n","print(\"Pit-lane starts (grid 0) from 2003:\", (history.loc[model_rows, \"grid\"] == 0).sum(),\n","      \"| podiums among them:\", history.loc[model_rows & (history[\"grid\"] == 0), \"podium\"].sum())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":63,"id":"cebbc970","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.24452Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.244008Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.411801Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.410424Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.207515,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.413908+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.206393+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 900x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Podium rate from grid 1, 2, 3 (%): [80.3, 62.7, 51.7]\n","Spearman correlation, grid_pos vs podium: -0.494\n"]}],"source":["# evidence only from the training seasons (2003-2019), so validation and test stay unseen\n","train_rows = (history[\"year\"] >= 2003) & (history[\"year\"] <= 2019)\n","by_grid = history[train_rows].groupby(\"grid_pos\")[\"podium\"].mean()\n","\n","ax = (100 * by_grid).plot(marker=\"o\", figsize=(9, 4))\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"starting position (pit lane counted as last)\")\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"podium rate (%)\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Podium rate by starting position, training seasons 2003-2019\")\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"Podium rate from grid 1, 2, 3 (%):\", (100 * by_grid.loc[1:3]).round(1).tolist())\n","print(\"Spearman correlation, grid_pos vs podium:\",\n","      round(history.loc[train_rows, \"grid_pos\"].corr(history.loc[train_rows, \"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"214b45d7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036964,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.48768+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.450716+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Starting position is strongly linked to a podium:** in the training seasons, 80.3% of drivers starting from pole finished on the podium, 62.7% from 2nd and 51.7% from 3rd. The rate falls quickly after that, to about 5% from 8th place, and is close to zero from 12th backwards. The rank correlation between starting position and podium is −0.49: the further back a driver starts, the less likely a podium.\n","2) **This matches the F1 introduction:** it calls pole position the \"strongest single predictor of a podium\", and our data agrees.\n","3) **The recode is safe:** from 2003 there are 73 pit-lane starts and none of them ended on the podium, so counting them as starting last puts them where their results are.\n","\n","**Our decision:** `grid_pos` is our first feature, forming the grid group. The relationship is clearly not a straight line (the drop from 1st to 4th is far larger than from 10th to 13th), which matters later: a linear model may need help with this shape, while tree models handle it on their own."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"de1348aa","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.036456,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.560599+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.524143+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.4 Qualifying\n","\n","`quali_pos` is the driver's position in the qualifying session, known before the race. 1.1 showed it is not the same as `grid`: penalties can move a driver back, and in 2021–2022 the sprint set the grid on sprint weekends. We check two things on the training seasons: whether the qualifying position is linked to a podium, and whether it tells us anything that `grid_pos` does not already tell us."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":64,"id":"f0db3040","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.636793Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.636259Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.830263Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.829102Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.234684,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.832348+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.597664+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 900x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows without a qualifying position: 20 of 6783\n","Spearman with podium: qualifying -0.497 | grid -0.494\n","Spearman between qualifying and grid: 0.97\n"]}],"source":["t = history[train_rows]\n","by_quali = t.groupby(\"quali_pos\")[\"podium\"].mean()\n","\n","ax = (100 * by_grid).plot(marker=\"o\", figsize=(9, 4), label=\"by starting position (grid)\")\n","(100 * by_quali).plot(ax=ax, marker=\"s\", label=\"by qualifying position\")\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"position\")\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"podium rate (%)\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Podium rate by grid and by qualifying position, training seasons 2003-2019\")\n","ax.legend()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"Rows without a qualifying position:\", t[\"quali_pos\"].isna().sum(), \"of\", len(t))\n","print(\"Spearman with podium: qualifying\", round(t[\"quali_pos\"].corr(t[\"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3),\n","      \"| grid\", round(t[\"grid_pos\"].corr(t[\"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3))\n","print(\"Spearman between qualifying and grid:\", round(t[\"quali_pos\"].corr(t[\"grid_pos\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":65,"id":"31dfd4ed","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.914786Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.913773Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.937963Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.936797Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.06697,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.940172+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.873202+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>size</th>\n","      <th>mean</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>grid_group</th>\n","      <th>start_vs_quali</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1-3</th>\n","      <th>started at or ahead of qualifying</th>\n","      <td>958</td>\n","      <td>0.649</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\">4-6</th>\n","      <th>started at or ahead of qualifying</th>\n","      <td>949</td>\n","      <td>0.230</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>started behind qualifying</th>\n","      <td>12</td>\n","      <td>0.083</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\">7-10</th>\n","      <th>started at or ahead of qualifying</th>\n","      <td>1234</td>\n","      <td>0.054</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>started behind qualifying</th>\n","      <td>44</td>\n","      <td>0.159</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\">11+</th>\n","      <th>started at or ahead of qualifying</th>\n","      <td>3228</td>\n","      <td>0.011</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>started behind qualifying</th>\n","      <td>338</td>\n","      <td>0.033</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                                              size   mean\n","grid_group start_vs_quali                                \n","1-3        started at or ahead of qualifying   958  0.649\n","4-6        started at or ahead of qualifying   949  0.230\n","           started behind qualifying            12  0.083\n","7-10       started at or ahead of qualifying  1234  0.054\n","           started behind qualifying            44  0.159\n","11+        started at or ahead of qualifying  3228  0.011\n","           started behind qualifying           338  0.033"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# compare drivers who start from the same grid group: did they qualify higher than they start?\n","t = history[train_rows & history[\"quali_pos\"].notna()].copy()\n","t[\"grid_group\"] = pd.cut(t[\"grid_pos\"], bins=[0, 3, 6, 10, 30], labels=[\"1-3\", \"4-6\", \"7-10\", \"11+\"])\n","t[\"start_vs_quali\"] = np.where(t[\"grid_pos\"] > t[\"quali_pos\"], \"started behind qualifying\",\n","                               \"started at or ahead of qualifying\")\n","display(t.groupby([\"grid_group\", \"start_vs_quali\"], observed=True)[\"podium\"].agg([\"size\", \"mean\"]).round(3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"268234a9","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.039657,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.019461+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:35.979804+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Qualifying is linked to a podium as strongly as the grid:** the two curves almost overlap (79.1% of pole-sitters in qualifying reached the podium, against 80.3% from pole on the grid), and the correlations with podium are almost equal (−0.497 for qualifying, −0.494 for grid). \n","2) **The two are very similar:** their rank correlation is 0.97. For most drivers the qualifying position and the starting position are the same or almost the same.\n","3) **But qualifying adds information when they differ:** among drivers starting 7th–10th, those who had qualified higher than they started reached the podium 15.9% of the time, against 5.4% for the others. From 11th or lower it is 3.3% against 1.1%. A driver moved back by a penalty is still faster than his starting slot suggests, and qualifying captures that. (The 4th–6th group has only 12 such drivers, too few to read anything into.)\n","4) **Almost complete:** only 20 of the 6,783 training rows have no qualifying position. They are handled with the other missing values in 3.8.\n","\n","**Our decision:** `quali_pos` is the qualifying group. Together with `grid_pos`, the model can see both how fast a driver was in qualifying and where he actually starts, and therefore also the gap between the two."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"edf62f08","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.040303,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.099211+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.058908+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.5 Rank before the race\n","\n","The F1 introduction names car performance as the dominant factor in who wins, and the championship standings summarise how strong a driver and a team have been so far in the season. But 1.1 showed that the standings stored for a race are the standings after it: they already contain that race's points. Using them for the same race would be leakage. Following the F1 introduction, we shift them to \"standings before this race\": for every race we take the standings after the previous race of the same season. The first race of a season has no earlier standings, so those rows are left empty. The row count before and after the joins, printed below, confirms that they add no rows."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":66,"id":"ea27ef41","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.184566Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.184134Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.236412Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.235329Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.098689,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.238473+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.139784+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rows before and after the joins: 24524 24524\n","Missing from 2003 (driver, team): 594 484 of 8910 | rows in a season's first race: 453\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>round</th>\n","      <th>positionOrder</th>\n","      <th>driver_rank_before</th>\n","      <th>team_rank_before</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17423</th>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>NaN</td>\n","      <td>NaN</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17449</th>\n","      <td>2</td>\n","      <td>5</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17479</th>\n","      <td>3</td>\n","      <td>13</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17491</th>\n","      <td>4</td>\n","      <td>3</td>\n","      <td>3.0</td>\n","      <td>3.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["       round  positionOrder  driver_rank_before  team_rank_before\n","17423      1              1                 NaN               NaN\n","17449      2              5                 1.0               1.0\n","17479      3             13                 1.0               1.0\n","17491      4              3                 3.0               3.0"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# for every race, the previous race of the same season (none for the first race)\n","races = clean[\"races\"][[\"raceId\", \"year\", \"round\"]].sort_values([\"year\", \"round\"])\n","races[\"prev_raceId\"] = races.groupby(\"year\")[\"raceId\"].shift(1)\n","history = history.merge(races[[\"raceId\", \"prev_raceId\"]], on=\"raceId\", how=\"left\")\n","\n","# standings after the previous race = standings before this race\n","driver_before = clean[\"driver_standings\"][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"position\"]].rename(\n","    columns={\"raceId\": \"prev_raceId\", \"position\": \"driver_rank_before\"})\n","team_before = clean[\"constructor_standings\"][[\"raceId\", \"constructorId\", \"position\"]].rename(\n","    columns={\"raceId\": \"prev_raceId\", \"position\": \"team_rank_before\"})\n","\n","rows_before = len(history)\n","history = (history.merge(driver_before, on=[\"prev_raceId\", \"driverId\"], how=\"left\")\n","                  .merge(team_before, on=[\"prev_raceId\", \"constructorId\"], how=\"left\"))\n","print(\"Rows before and after the joins:\", rows_before, len(history))\n","\n","model_rows = history[\"year\"] >= 2003\n","print(\"Missing from 2003 (driver, team):\", history.loc[model_rows, \"driver_rank_before\"].isna().sum(),\n","      history.loc[model_rows, \"team_rank_before\"].isna().sum(), \"of\", model_rows.sum(),\n","      \"| rows in a season's first race:\", history.loc[model_rows, \"prev_raceId\"].isna().sum())\n","\n","# check the shift on one driver: Hamilton (driverId 1), first races of 2008\n","display(history[(history[\"year\"] == 2008) & (history[\"driverId\"] == 1)]\n","        [[\"round\", \"positionOrder\", \"driver_rank_before\", \"team_rank_before\"]].head(4))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":67,"id":"4ffa4a06","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.321857Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.321054Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.679377Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.678192Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.402401,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.681545+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.279144+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x400 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Spearman with podium, driver_rank_before: -0.478 | with grid_pos: 0.726\n","Spearman with podium, team_rank_before: -0.447 | with grid_pos: 0.708\n"]}],"source":["# history now has new columns, so rebuild the training-season mask\n","train_rows = (history[\"year\"] >= 2003) & (history[\"year\"] <= 2019)\n","t = history[train_rows]\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4))\n","(100 * t.groupby(\"driver_rank_before\")[\"podium\"].mean()).plot(ax=axes[0], marker=\"o\")\n","axes[0].set_title(\"Podium rate by driver's championship rank before the race\")\n","axes[0].set_xlabel(\"driver's championship rank before the race\")\n","axes[0].set_ylabel(\"podium rate (%)\")\n","(100 * t.groupby(\"team_rank_before\")[\"podium\"].mean()).plot(ax=axes[1], marker=\"o\", color=\"darkorange\")\n","axes[1].set_title(\"Podium rate by team's championship rank before the race\")\n","axes[1].set_xlabel(\"team's championship rank before the race\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","for col in [\"driver_rank_before\", \"team_rank_before\"]:\n","    print(f\"Spearman with podium, {col}:\", round(t[col].corr(t[\"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3),\n","          \"| with grid_pos:\", round(t[col].corr(t[\"grid_pos\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"62e5bf28","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.042113,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.76858+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.726467+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The shift works:** Hamilton won the first race of 2008. His standing before that race is empty, and before the second race he is 1st, exactly the result of the first race. Every row only sees races that have already happened.\n","2) **Strong drivers and teams reach the podium far more often:** in the training seasons, the driver leading the championship before a race finished on the podium 67.7% of the time, the 2nd 57.4% and the 3rd 41.5%. For teams it is 58.9% for the leading team, 40.0% for the 2nd, 26.3% for the 3rd, and only 4.3% for the 5th. The correlations with podium are −0.48 (driver) and −0.45 (team).\n","3) **Related to the grid, but not the same:** the correlation with the starting position is about 0.7, far below the 0.97 between qualifying and grid. The standings describe the whole season so far, while the grid describes one Saturday, so they can add something to each other. The F1 introduction names car performance as the dominant factor, and the hybrid era shows that the constructor explains most of the variation in results, which supports keeping the team standing.\n","4) **Missing values have a clear cause:** 594 of the 8,910 modeling rows have no driver standing and 484 no team standing. 453 of them are first races of a season, where no standings exist yet; the rest are drivers or teams with no standing entry before that race. They are handled in 3.8.\n","\n","**Our decision:** `driver_rank_before` and `team_rank_before` form the standings group."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a1ac707b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.04196,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.852023+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.810063+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.6 Recent form\n","\n","The standings in 3.5 only cover the current season and are empty at its first race. Form fills that gap: it measures how often a driver, and separately his team, reached the podium in their most recent races, including races from the previous season.\n","\n","The brief requires this feature to use only past races. We therefore sort all races by date and, for every row, look only at the races before it: the current race is never included. Driver form is the share of a driver's previous races that ended on the podium. Team form is the share of the team's cars that finished on the podium in the team's previous races. A driver or team with no earlier race has no form value.\n","\n","How many past races should form cover? Too few and it reacts to luck, too many and it remembers seasons that no longer matter. We try 3, 5 and 10 races on the training seasons and keep the one most closely linked to a podium."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":68,"id":"9cbc2c46","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.940629Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.940083Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:37.954465Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:37.953472Z"},"papermill":{"duration":1.060588,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:37.957119+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:36.896531+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>previous races</th>\n","      <th>driver form vs podium</th>\n","      <th>team form vs podium</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>0</th>\n","      <td>3</td>\n","      <td>0.511</td>\n","      <td>0.513</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>5</td>\n","      <td>0.526</td>\n","      <td>0.515</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>2</th>\n","      <td>10</td>\n","      <td>0.519</td>\n","      <td>0.502</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["   previous races  driver form vs podium  team form vs podium\n","0               3                  0.511                0.513\n","1               5                  0.526                0.515\n","2              10                  0.519                0.502"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["history = history.sort_values([\"date\", \"raceId\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n","train_rows = (history[\"year\"] >= 2003) & (history[\"year\"] <= 2019)\n","\n","def form(n):\n","    \"\"\"Podium share over each driver's and each team's previous n races (never the current race).\"\"\"\n","    past = lambda s: s.shift(1).rolling(n, min_periods=1).mean()\n","    driver = history.groupby(\"driverId\")[\"podium\"].transform(past)\n","    team_races = history.groupby([\"date\", \"raceId\", \"constructorId\"], as_index=False)[\"podium\"].mean()\n","    team_races[\"team_form\"] = team_races.groupby(\"constructorId\")[\"podium\"].transform(past)\n","    team = history[[\"raceId\", \"constructorId\"]].merge(team_races, on=[\"raceId\", \"constructorId\"], how=\"left\")[\"team_form\"]\n","    return driver, team\n","\n","compare = []\n","for n in [3, 5, 10]:\n","    driver, team = form(n)\n","    compare.append({\"previous races\": n,\n","                    \"driver form vs podium\": round(driver[train_rows].corr(history.loc[train_rows, \"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3),\n","                    \"team form vs podium\": round(team[train_rows].corr(history.loc[train_rows, \"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3)})\n","display(pd.DataFrame(compare))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":69,"id":"54468fb0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.044794Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.044269Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.562751Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.561955Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.564506,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.564698+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.000192+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Missing from 2003 (driver, team): 89 41 of 8910\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>round</th>\n","      <th>podium</th>\n","      <th>driver_form</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17423</th>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>0.4</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17449</th>\n","      <td>2</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>0.4</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17479</th>\n","      <td>3</td>\n","      <td>0</td>\n","      <td>0.4</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17491</th>\n","      <td>4</td>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>0.2</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17512</th>\n","      <td>5</td>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>0.4</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>17531</th>\n","      <td>6</td>\n","      <td>1</td>\n","      <td>0.6</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["       round  podium  driver_form\n","17423      1       1          0.4\n","17449      2       0          0.4\n","17479      3       0          0.4\n","17491      4       1          0.2\n","17512      5       1          0.4\n","17531      6       1          0.6"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["history[\"driver_form\"], history[\"team_form\"] = form(5)\n","\n","model_rows = history[\"year\"] >= 2003\n","print(\"Missing from 2003 (driver, team):\", history.loc[model_rows, \"driver_form\"].isna().sum(),\n","      history.loc[model_rows, \"team_form\"].isna().sum(), \"of\", model_rows.sum())\n","\n","# check on one driver: Hamilton (driverId 1) in 2008\n","display(history[(history[\"year\"] == 2008) & (history[\"driverId\"] == 1)][[\"round\", \"podium\", \"driver_form\"]].head(6))"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":70,"id":"71874796","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.649866Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.649381Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.003062Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.002006Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.399459,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.005258+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:38.605799+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x400 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Spearman with podium, driver_form: 0.526 | with grid_pos: -0.569 | with team_rank_before: -0.683\n","Spearman with podium, team_form: 0.515 | with grid_pos: -0.613 | with team_rank_before: -0.768\n"]}],"source":["t = history[train_rows]\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4))\n","(100 * t.groupby((t[\"driver_form\"] * 5).round() / 5)[\"podium\"].mean()).plot(ax=axes[0], marker=\"o\")\n","axes[0].set_title(\"Podium rate by driver form (last 5 races)\")\n","axes[0].set_xlabel(\"share of the driver's last 5 races on the podium\")\n","axes[0].set_ylabel(\"podium rate (%)\")\n","(100 * t.groupby(t[\"team_form\"].round(1))[\"podium\"].mean()).plot(ax=axes[1], marker=\"o\", color=\"darkorange\")\n","axes[1].set_title(\"Podium rate by team form (last 5 races)\")\n","axes[1].set_xlabel(\"share of the team's cars on the podium in its last 5 races\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","for col in [\"driver_form\", \"team_form\"]:\n","    print(f\"Spearman with podium, {col}:\", round(t[col].corr(t[\"podium\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3),\n","          \"| with grid_pos:\", round(t[col].corr(t[\"grid_pos\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3),\n","          \"| with team_rank_before:\", round(t[col].corr(t[\"team_rank_before\"], method=\"spearman\"), 3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d5298f19","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.04334,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.091082+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.047742+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Five past races work best:** form over the last 5 races is slightly more closely linked to a podium than 3 or 10 races (0.526 against 0.511 and 0.519 for drivers), so we use 5. The differences are small, which also means the exact choice is not critical.\n","2) **Only past races are used:** Hamilton's form before the first race of 2008 is 0.4, his 2 podiums in the last 5 races of 2007, and it does not change because he won that race: the race itself is never counted. Form also carries over from one season to the next, which the standings cannot do.\n","3) **Form is strongly linked to a podium:** in the training seasons, a driver with no podium in his last 5 races reached the podium only 2.9% of the time, against 69.1% for a driver with 5 out of 5. The correlations with podium (0.53 for drivers, 0.52 for teams) are as strong as for the grid.\n","4) **It overlaps with the other groups but does not copy them:** form is related to the grid (about −0.6) and to the team standing (−0.68 and −0.77), since good teams start at the front and score points. But none of these correlations is close to the 0.97 between qualifying and grid, so form still carries its own information about recent results.\n","5) **Few missing values:** 89 rows have no driver form and 41 no team form, from a driver's or a team's first race, where no earlier race exists. They are handled in 3.8.\n","\n","**Our decision:** `driver_form` and `team_form` form the form group."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"85c75cab","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.042099,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.17577+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.133671+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.7 The feature set and the split\n","\n","Sections 3.3–3.6 give six features in four groups, all known before the race:\n","\n","| Group | Features | Evidence |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| Grid | `grid_pos` | 3.3: podium rate falls from 80.3% on pole to about 5% from 8th |\n","| Qualifying | `quali_pos` | 3.4: as strong as the grid, and adds information when a penalty moves a driver back |\n","| Standings | `driver_rank_before`, `team_rank_before` | 3.5: championship leaders reach the podium 67.7% (driver) and 58.9% (team) of the time |\n","| Form | `driver_form`, `team_form` | 3.6: no podium in the last 5 races gives 2.9%, five out of five gives 69.1% |\n","\n","Two candidates are left out on purpose. A home-race feature is not included because Q2 found no home advantage once starting position is taken into account. Sprint results are not used because, as noted in 1.1, they exist only from 2021, so the training seasons contain none.\n","\n","We split the 2003–2024 rows by season, following the boundaries in the F1 introduction: training 2003–2019, validation 2020–2021 and test 2022–2024. A split by time, rather than a random one, matches how the model would be used: it learns from past seasons and predicts later ones. A random split would put rows from the same race, and from later seasons, into training, so the model would partly be tested on races it had already seen. The validation seasons are used to choose settings and the decision threshold, and the test seasons are used only once, for the final scores."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":71,"id":"701f17b5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.264054Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.263703Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.307695Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.306671Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.089298,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.309866+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.220568+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>seasons</th>\n","      <th>races</th>\n","      <th>rows</th>\n","      <th>podium_rate</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>split</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>train</th>\n","      <td>2003-2019</td>\n","      <td>321</td>\n","      <td>6783</td>\n","      <td>14.2</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>2020-2021</td>\n","      <td>39</td>\n","      <td>775</td>\n","      <td>15.1</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>2022-2024</td>\n","      <td>68</td>\n","      <td>1352</td>\n","      <td>15.1</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["              seasons  races  rows  podium_rate\n","split                                          \n","train       2003-2019    321  6783         14.2\n","validation  2020-2021     39   775         15.1\n","test        2022-2024     68  1352         15.1"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Races in more than one split: 0\n","Missing values per split (%):\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>grid_pos</th>\n","      <th>quali_pos</th>\n","      <th>driver_rank_before</th>\n","      <th>team_rank_before</th>\n","      <th>driver_form</th>\n","      <th>team_form</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>split</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>train</th>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.3</td>\n","      <td>7.1</td>\n","      <td>5.7</td>\n","      <td>1.1</td>\n","      <td>0.5</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.1</td>\n","      <td>5.5</td>\n","      <td>5.2</td>\n","      <td>0.8</td>\n","      <td>0.5</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>5.0</td>\n","      <td>4.4</td>\n","      <td>0.6</td>\n","      <td>0.1</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["            grid_pos  quali_pos  driver_rank_before  team_rank_before  \\\n","split                                                                   \n","train            0.0        0.3                 7.1               5.7   \n","validation       0.0        0.1                 5.5               5.2   \n","test             0.0        0.0                 5.0               4.4   \n","\n","            driver_form  team_form  \n","split                               \n","train               1.1        0.5  \n","validation          0.8        0.5  \n","test                0.6        0.1  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["FEATURE_GROUPS = {\"grid\": [\"grid_pos\"], \"qualifying\": [\"quali_pos\"],\n","                  \"standings\": [\"driver_rank_before\", \"team_rank_before\"],\n","                  \"form\": [\"driver_form\", \"team_form\"]}\n","FEATURES = [f for group in FEATURE_GROUPS.values() for f in group]\n","\n","model_table = history[history[\"year\"] >= 2003][[\"raceId\", \"driverId\", \"year\"] + FEATURES + [\"podium\"]].copy()\n","model_table[\"split\"] = np.select([model_table[\"year\"] <= 2019, model_table[\"year\"] <= 2021],\n","                                 [\"train\", \"validation\"], default=\"test\")\n","\n","summary = model_table.groupby(\"split\", sort=False).agg(seasons=(\"year\", lambda y: f\"{y.min()}-{y.max()}\"),\n","                                                        races=(\"raceId\", \"nunique\"), rows=(\"podium\", \"size\"),\n","                                                        podium_rate=(\"podium\", \"mean\"))\n","summary[\"podium_rate\"] = (100 * summary[\"podium_rate\"]).round(1)\n","display(summary)\n","print(\"Races in more than one split:\", (model_table.groupby(\"raceId\")[\"split\"].nunique() > 1).sum())\n","print(\"Missing values per split (%):\")\n","display((100 * model_table.groupby(\"split\", sort=False)[FEATURES].apply(lambda g: g.isna().mean())).round(1))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"453be272","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.04228,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.39377+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.35149+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Sizes:** training has 6,783 rows from 321 races (76.1% of the modeling table), validation 775 rows from 39 races (8.7%), and test 1,352 rows from 68 races (15.2%). No race is split across two sets.\n","2) **Podiums are equally common in every split:** 14.2% in training and 15.1% in validation and test, close to the 3-out-of-20 of a modern grid. The model is evaluated on the same kind of target it learns from.\n","3) **Missing values are few and of one main kind:** apart from the standings (5–7%, mostly first races of a season), every feature is missing for at most about 1% of rows. These are handled in 3.8.\n","4) **Using earlier test races as history is not leakage:** the form and standings of a 2023 race use results from 2022 races, which belong to the test set. At prediction time those races are already over, so a real forecast would know them too. What the model never sees is the result of the race it predicts.\n","5) **The test seasons are a new era:** 2022 brought new car rules (the ground-effect era in the F1 introduction), so the test checks whether what the model learned in 2003–2019 still holds. We report this as a limitation.\n","6) **Why these sizes:** the split follows season boundaries, so the percentages follow from the seasons rather than being chosen. Validation is the smallest part (8.7%) because it covers only two seasons, one of them the COVID-shortened 2020 season with 17 races. Its 39 races still contain 117 podiums, enough to choose the threshold and settings, but its scores are less stable than those of a larger set, which we keep in mind when comparing models."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2b7178f9","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.041535,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.477563+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.436028+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3.8 Preprocessing\n","\n","Two steps prepare the features for the models: filling the missing values and putting the features on a common scale. Both are learned from the training seasons only and then applied unchanged to validation and test, so no information from later seasons leaks into the preparation.\n","\n","**Missing values.** 3.4–3.6 left a small number of gaps, each with a known cause. We fill them according to what they mean:\n","1) **Qualifying position:** a driver without a qualifying position gets his starting position instead. 3.4 showed that the two agree almost completely (rank correlation 0.97), so the grid is the best available stand-in.\n","2) **Standings and form:** these are missing at a season's first race (standings) or at a driver's or team's first race (form). They are filled with the median of the training seasons, which Lab 1 recommends for numerical features because, unlike the mean, it is not pulled by extreme values.\n","\n","**Scaling.** Logistic regression and the neural network are sensitive to features on different scales: a championship rank runs from 1 to 27, while form runs from 0 to 1. Standardisation gives every feature a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1 on the training seasons. Tree models do not need this, so they use the filled but unscaled values."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":72,"id":"ec85026d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.566716Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.565625Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.588747Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.587473Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.070164,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.590864+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.5207+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Grid position of training rows without qualifying: 19 to 24\n","Training medians used for the other gaps: {'driver_rank_before': 11.0, 'team_rank_before': 6.0, 'driver_form': 0.0, 'team_form': 0.0}\n","Missing values before: 1229 | after: 0\n"]}],"source":["train = model_table[model_table[\"split\"] == \"train\"]\n","MEDIANS = train[FEATURES].median()\n","\n","def fill_missing(df):\n","    \"\"\"Missing qualifying -> the driver's grid position; every other gap -> the training median.\"\"\"\n","    df = df.copy()\n","    df[\"quali_pos\"] = df[\"quali_pos\"].fillna(df[\"grid_pos\"])\n","    df[FEATURES] = df[FEATURES].fillna(MEDIANS)\n","    return df\n","\n","no_quali = train[\"quali_pos\"].isna()\n","print(\"Grid position of training rows without qualifying:\",\n","      train.loc[no_quali, \"grid_pos\"].min(), \"to\", train.loc[no_quali, \"grid_pos\"].max())\n","print(\"Training medians used for the other gaps:\", MEDIANS.drop([\"grid_pos\", \"quali_pos\"]).to_dict())\n","\n","filled = fill_missing(model_table)\n","print(\"Missing values before:\", model_table[FEATURES].isna().sum().sum(), \"| after:\", filled[FEATURES].isna().sum().sum())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":73,"id":"56b5cd9d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.679613Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.679301Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.490231Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.48884Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.859593,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.492649+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:39.633056+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>mean before</th>\n","      <th>std before</th>\n","      <th>mean after</th>\n","      <th>std after</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>grid_pos</th>\n","      <td>11.18</td>\n","      <td>6.23</td>\n","      <td>-0.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>quali_pos</th>\n","      <td>11.18</td>\n","      <td>6.23</td>\n","      <td>-0.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>driver_rank_before</th>\n","      <td>11.25</td>\n","      <td>6.22</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>team_rank_before</th>\n","      <td>5.84</td>\n","      <td>3.02</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>driver_form</th>\n","      <td>0.14</td>\n","      <td>0.25</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>team_form</th>\n","      <td>0.14</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>1.0</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                    mean before  std before  mean after  std after\n","grid_pos                  11.18        6.23        -0.0        1.0\n","quali_pos                 11.18        6.23        -0.0        1.0\n","driver_rank_before        11.25        6.22         0.0        1.0\n","team_rank_before           5.84        3.02         0.0        1.0\n","driver_form                0.14        0.25         0.0        1.0\n","team_form                  0.14        0.23         0.0        1.0"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x400 with 3 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n","\n","scaler = StandardScaler().fit(filled.loc[filled[\"split\"] == \"train\", FEATURES])\n","scaled = filled.copy()\n","scaled[FEATURES] = scaler.transform(filled[FEATURES])\n","\n","tr = filled[\"split\"] == \"train\"\n","display(pd.DataFrame({\"mean before\": filled.loc[tr, FEATURES].mean(), \"std before\": filled.loc[tr, FEATURES].std(),\n","                      \"mean after\": scaled.loc[tr, FEATURES].mean(), \"std after\": scaled.loc[tr, FEATURES].std()}).round(2))\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 4))\n","axes[0].hist(model_table.loc[tr, \"driver_rank_before\"].dropna(), bins=27)\n","axes[0].set_title(\"driver_rank_before, raw (gaps left out)\")\n","axes[1].hist(filled.loc[tr, \"driver_rank_before\"], bins=27, color=\"darkorange\")\n","axes[1].set_title(\"after filling gaps with the median (11)\")\n","axes[2].hist(scaled.loc[tr, \"driver_rank_before\"], bins=27, color=\"green\")\n","axes[2].set_title(\"after scaling (mean 0, std 1)\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"dd166bc4","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.042896,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.58076+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.537864+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **All gaps are filled:** 1,229 missing values before, none after.\n","2) **The qualifying gaps belong to drivers at the back:** every training row without a qualifying position started between 19th and 24th. Filling with the grid keeps them at the back, where a median of 11 would have moved them to midfield.\n","3) **The median fill leaves a visible mark:** for the driver standing, the gaps (mostly first races of a season) all become rank 11, which shows as a tall bar in the middle of the histogram. Filling them with the last rank instead would be wrong: drivers without a standing reach the podium 11.8% of the time, close to the 14.2% average, against 0.1% for drivers ranked 20th or worse. They are unknown, not weak. The median is a neutral guess, but it still understates them (real rank-11 drivers reach the podium only 3.5% of the time), which we report as a limitation in Section 8. For form, the median is 0, so a newcomer is treated as having no recent podiums, which matches most debut races.\n","4) **Scaling changes the range, not the shape:** after standardisation every feature has a mean of 0 and a standard deviation of 1 on the training seasons, while the shape of each distribution stays the same. Validation and test are transformed with the training values, so their means are close to, but not exactly, 0.\n","\n","**Our decision:** `filled` (gaps filled, original scale) is used by the tree models, and `scaled` (gaps filled and standardised) by logistic regression and the neural network. Both steps are learned from the training seasons only."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":74,"id":"c605df6f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.671004Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.670354Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.474123Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.473151Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.852438,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.476699+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:40.624261+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x600 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["import seaborn as sns\n","\n","corr = model_table.loc[model_table[\"split\"] == \"train\", FEATURES + [\"podium\"]].corr(method=\"spearman\")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\n","sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, fmt=\".2f\", cmap=\"coolwarm\", vmin=-1, vmax=1)\n","plt.title(\"Spearman correlation between the features and podium, training seasons 2003-2019\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e41d0f01","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.043363,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.566523+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.52316+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Every feature is about equally linked to a podium:** the correlations with `podium` lie between 0.45 and 0.53 in size. Positions and ranks are negative (a smaller number is better), form is positive (a higher share is better).\n","2) **Some features overlap strongly:** qualifying and grid (0.97), the driver's and the team's standing (0.88), and driver and team form (0.87). Overlapping features carry much of the same information, so a model may rely on either one of a pair. This matters when we read feature importance in Section 6: importance can be shared between two overlapping features, so a low score for one of them does not mean that information is useless."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0eced22f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.044441,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.654811+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.61037+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# 4. Predictive Modeling\n","\n","We train three kinds of models on the same modeling table (same rows, same six features), so their scores can be compared directly:\n","- **Logistic regression**: our baseline, the simplest reasonable model.\n","- **Tree models** (random forest ): the second family of statistical models.\n","- **A shallow neural network** with 1–2 hidden layers.\n","\n","Every model is scored on train, validation and test with ROC-AUC, PR-AUC, F1, precision and recall. The probability threshold that turns a probability into a yes/no answer is chosen on the validation seasons only. The test seasons (2022–2024) are used only to report the final scores."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1f4f3182","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.044295,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.744127+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.699832+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4.1 Training inputs and how we evaluate\n","\n","Every model learns from the same rows and the same six features. Tree models use `filled` (gaps filled, original units). Logistic regression and the neural network use `scaled` (same values after StandardScaler). First we separate the inputs by split and check how common a podium is in each one."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":75,"id":"4ee90436","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.834378Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.834042Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.861923Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.860539Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.075996,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.864351+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.788355+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["            rows  podiums  podium rate %\n","train       6783      963           14.2\n","validation   775      117           15.1\n","test        1352      204           15.1\n"]}],"source":["SPLITS = [\"train\", \"validation\", \"test\"]\n","y = {s: filled.loc[filled[\"split\"] == s, \"podium\"] for s in SPLITS}\n","X_filled = {s: filled.loc[filled[\"split\"] == s, FEATURES] for s in SPLITS}\n","X_scaled = {s: scaled.loc[scaled[\"split\"] == s, FEATURES] for s in SPLITS}\n","\n","print(pd.DataFrame({\"rows\": {s: len(y[s]) for s in SPLITS},\n","                    \"podiums\": {s: y[s].sum() for s in SPLITS},\n","                    \"podium rate %\": {s: round(100 * y[s].mean(), 1) for s in SPLITS}}))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"de920a44","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.043721,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.955721+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:41.912+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Same rows as 3.7:** 6,783 training, 775 validation and 1,352 test rows.\n","2) **Podiums are rare:** about 15% of rows in every split. The counts are exactly 3 per race (321, 39 and 68 races), so the target is the same in every split."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":76,"id":"1a5d44d9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.047821Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.047309Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.160404Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.159497Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.161755,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.162596+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.000841+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, roc_auc_score, average_precision_score, f1_score, precision_score, recall_score\n","\n","def scores(y_true, prob, threshold):\n","    pred = (prob >= threshold).astype(int)\n","    return {\"Accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_true, pred),\n","            \"ROC-AUC\": roc_auc_score(y_true, prob), \"PR-AUC\": average_precision_score(y_true, prob),\n","            \"F1\": f1_score(y_true, pred, zero_division=0), \"Precision\": precision_score(y_true, pred, zero_division=0),\n","            \"Recall\": recall_score(y_true, pred, zero_division=0)}\n","\n","def best_threshold(y_true, prob):\n","    thresholds = np.round(np.arange(0.05, 0.95, 0.01), 2)\n","    f1s = [f1_score(y_true, prob >= t, zero_division=0) for t in thresholds]\n","    return thresholds[np.argmax(f1s)]\n","\n","results = {}\n","def evaluate(name, probs):\n","    threshold = best_threshold(y[\"validation\"], probs[\"validation\"])\n","    table = pd.DataFrame({s: scores(y[s], probs[s], threshold) for s in SPLITS}).T.round(3)\n","    table[\"threshold\"] = threshold\n","    results[name] = table\n","    return table"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2586bac3","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.044467,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.251415+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.206948+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Accuracy fools us:** podiums are rare, about 15% of rows, so a model that always answered \"no podium\" would already be right for about 85% of the rows (84.9% in validation and test) without finding a single podium: its recall and F1 would be 0. Accuracy rewards saying \"no\", so we do not use it to compare models. This is the same problem as the cats-and-dogs example in Lab 2 (p.4).\n","\n","2) **The metrics we use instead:**\n","   - **Precision:** when the model says \"podium\", how often it is right (false alarms lower it).\n","   - **Recall:** of all real podiums, how many the model finds (missed podiums lower it).\n","   - **F1:** combines precision and recall into one number. It is only high when both are high, so it cannot be cheated by saying \"podium\" for everyone (high recall, low precision) or for almost no one (high precision, low recall).\n","   - **ROC-AUC:** the chance that the model gives a random podium driver a higher probability than a random non-podium driver. 0.5 is a coin flip, 1.0 is perfect.\n","   - **PR-AUC:** how precise the model stays as it finds more and more of the podiums, over all possible thresholds. A model with no skill gets the podium rate (about 0.15), and a perfect model gets 1.0.\n","\n","3) **The floor every model must beat:** a model with no skill cannot rank drivers at all, because it gives everyone the same probability. Its ROC-AUC is therefore 0.5, and its PR-AUC equals the podium rate of each split (0.142 in training, 0.151 in validation and test). A real model is only useful if it scores clearly above these numbers.\n","\n","4) **Our metric choice:**\n","   - **Primary metric: PR-AUC.** Podiums are rare, and the brief notes that PR-AUC is more informative than ROC-AUC in this case. ROC-AUC also counts the many easy \"no podium\" answers in the model's favour, while PR-AUC only judges the podium predictions. It also does not depend on any threshold.\n","   - **Secondary metric: F1.** It scores the actual yes/no answers the model gives at the threshold we choose.\n","   - **ROC-AUC, precision and recall** are reported as well. The brief asks for five metrics while its table lists three, so we add precision and recall, the two parts of F1.\n","\n","5) **The threshold:** a model outputs a probability, and the threshold decides from which probability we answer \"podium\" (Lab 2, p.2). We try every value from 0.05 to 0.94 and keep the one with the best F1 on the validation seasons. The test seasons are never used for this, as the brief requires. "]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b3c6dd3d","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.045547,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.341367+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.29582+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4.2 Baseline: logistic regression\n","\n","Our baseline is logistic regression, the simplest reasonable model for a yes/no target. It gives each feature a weight, adds up weight × feature value for a driver, and passes the sum through the sigmoid function, which turns it into a probability between 0 and 1 (Lab 2, p.2). Training finds the weights that best match the podiums in the training seasons. It uses the scaled features, so every weight is measured on the same scale. Every later model has to beat this baseline to justify its extra complexity."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":77,"id":"f5b9b0c4","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.434122Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.433526Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.610785Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.609577Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.22645,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.613594+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.387144+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Learned weights (scaled features):\n","grid_pos             -0.883\n","quali_pos            -0.986\n","driver_rank_before   -0.432\n","team_rank_before     -0.154\n","driver_form           0.349\n","team_form             0.136\n","dtype: float64\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","\n","lr = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n","lr.fit(X_scaled[\"train\"], y[\"train\"])\n","\n","lr_probs = {s: lr.predict_proba(X_scaled[s])[:, 1] for s in SPLITS}\n","\n","print(\"Learned weights (scaled features):\")\n","print(pd.Series(lr.coef_[0], index=FEATURES).round(3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"fa8da338","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.053769,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.749571+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.695802+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The directions make sense:** positions and ranks get negative weights (a smaller number, such as pole position, raises the probability), and form gets positive weights (more recent podiums raise it). This matches the correlations in the heatmap.\n","2) **Qualifying and grid carry the most weight**, followed by the driver's championship rank and driver form. Because the features are scaled, the sizes can be compared.\n","3) **Weights are not causes:** they show what the model relies on, not what causes a podium. Grid and qualifying overlap strongly (0.97), so the model can split the weight between them in many ways. We study importance properly in Section 6."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":78,"id":"2c877b29","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.844024Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.843331Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.296192Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.295189Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.502438,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.298139+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:42.795701+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Accuracy</th>\n","      <th>ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>F1</th>\n","      <th>Precision</th>\n","      <th>Recall</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>train</th>\n","      <td>0.879</td>\n","      <td>0.926</td>\n","      <td>0.680</td>\n","      <td>0.665</td>\n","      <td>0.549</td>\n","      <td>0.843</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.897</td>\n","      <td>0.927</td>\n","      <td>0.712</td>\n","      <td>0.699</td>\n","      <td>0.624</td>\n","      <td>0.795</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.871</td>\n","      <td>0.935</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.668</td>\n","      <td>0.545</td>\n","      <td>0.863</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["            Accuracy  ROC-AUC  PR-AUC     F1  Precision  Recall  threshold\n","train          0.879    0.926   0.680  0.665      0.549   0.843       0.23\n","validation     0.897    0.927   0.712  0.699      0.624   0.795       0.23\n","test           0.871    0.935   0.706  0.668      0.545   0.863       0.23"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Validation scores with the usual 0.5 threshold instead: {'Accuracy': 0.907, 'ROC-AUC': 0.927, 'PR-AUC': 0.712, 'F1': 0.667, 'Precision': 0.727, 'Recall': 0.615}\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix\n","\n","display(evaluate(\"Logistic regression\", lr_probs))\n","\n","threshold = results[\"Logistic regression\"][\"threshold\"].iloc[0]\n","print(\"Validation scores with the usual 0.5 threshold instead:\",\n","      {k: round(float(v), 3) for k, v in scores(y[\"validation\"], lr_probs[\"validation\"], 0.5).items()})\n","\n","cm = confusion_matrix(y[\"validation\"], (lr_probs[\"validation\"] >= threshold).astype(int))\n","sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\",\n","            xticklabels=[\"predicted no\", \"predicted podium\"], yticklabels=[\"really no\", \"really podium\"])\n","plt.title(f\"Logistic regression, validation seasons, threshold {threshold}\")\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8d67d051","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.047733,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.391592+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.343859+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","**1) Reading the confusion matrix (validation seasons, threshold 0.23)**\n","\n","The 775 validation rows fall into four boxes:\n","\n","| | Predicted no | Predicted podium |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **Really no podium** | 602 correct \"no\" (true negatives) | 56 false alarms (false positives) |\n","| **Really podium** | 24 missed podiums (false negatives) | 93 correct hits (true positives) |\n","\n","Every metric in the table is calculated from these four numbers:\n","- **Precision = 93 / (93 + 56) = 0.624.** When the model says \"podium\", it is right 62% of the time. The 56 false alarms pull it down.\n","- **Recall = 93 / (93 + 24) = 0.795.** The model finds 93 of the 117 real podiums, about 4 out of 5. The 24 misses pull it down.\n","- **F1 = 0.699**, the balance of the two (2 × 0.624 × 0.795 / (0.624 + 0.795)). It is only high when precision and recall are both reasonably high.\n","- **Accuracy = (602 + 93) / 775 = 0.897.** This looks impressive, but always answering \"no\" would already give 0.849, so accuracy rises by only 5 points while F1 rises from 0 to 0.699. This is why we do not use accuracy.\n","\n","The model says \"podium\" 149 times (93 + 56) in 39 races, about 3.8 per race, a little more than the 3 real podium places.\n","\n","**2) The threshold-free scores: far above the floor**\n","- **PR-AUC 0.712 against the no-skill level of 0.151**, almost five times higher. Across all thresholds, the model keeps its podium predictions precise while finding most podiums.\n","- **ROC-AUC 0.927 against 0.5.** If we take one random driver who finished on the podium and one who did not, the model gives the podium driver the higher probability 92.7% of the time.\n","\n","**3) Why the threshold is 0.23 and not 0.5**\n","With 0.5 the model says \"podium\" only when it is quite sure. It becomes more precise (0.727) but misses many more podiums (recall 0.615), and F1 falls to 0.667. At 0.23 it accepts a few more false alarms, finds many more podiums, and F1 rises to 0.699. Podiums are rare, so the model's probabilities are mostly low, and a lower cut-off works better. Note that PR-AUC and ROC-AUC are the same for both thresholds (0.712 and 0.927), because they do not depend on the threshold. The threshold was chosen on validation only.\n","\n","**4) No overfitting**\n","Training and validation scores are close: PR-AUC 0.680 against 0.712, and ROC-AUC 0.926 against 0.927. A model that memorised the training seasons would score clearly higher on training than on validation. Here validation is even slightly higher, which is normal variation for a set of only 39 races.\n","\n","**5) It holds on the unseen test seasons**\n","On 2022–2024, which the model never saw and which brought new car rules, PR-AUC is 0.706 and ROC-AUC 0.935, about the same as on validation. With the same threshold, recall goes up (0.863) and precision goes down (0.545): the model finds more podiums in the test seasons but also raises more false alarms. F1 is 0.668, slightly below validation. This is expected, because the threshold was tuned on validation, not on test.\n","\n","**6) Limitation**\n","Logistic regression adds the features up in a straight-line way. In 3.3 the podium rate dropped steeply from 1st to 4th on the grid but barely changed from 10th to 13th, a curved shape this model cannot follow exactly. Tree models can, which is why we try them next and compare them to this baseline."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c5bccd10","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.045942,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.485518+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.439576+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4.3 Random forest\n","\n","A random forest combines many decision trees (Lab 4, p.9). Each tree learns if-then rules from a random sample of the training rows and features, and the forest's podium probability is the share of trees that vote \"podium\". Unlike logistic regression, trees can follow curved relationships, such as the steep drop in podium rate over the first grid positions seen in 3.3. Trees do not need scaled features, so the forest uses `filled`.\n","\n","**Hyperparameter.** The main risk of a forest is overfitting: with no limit, a tree can grow a rule for a single driver in a single race and simply memorise the training seasons. `min_samples_leaf` sets how many training rows every final rule must cover. We try several values, and keep the one with the highest validation PR-AUC. The test seasons play no part in this choice. The number of trees is fixed at 300: more trees make the vote more stable but do not change what each tree learns."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":79,"id":"67b19bc3","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.581581Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.58109Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.44387Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.442772Z"},"papermill":{"duration":12.915813,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.446313+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:43.5305+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>train PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>validation PR-AUC</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>min_samples_leaf</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>1</th>\n","      <td>0.962</td>\n","      <td>0.624</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>5</th>\n","      <td>0.800</td>\n","      <td>0.705</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>10</th>\n","      <td>0.760</td>\n","      <td>0.722</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>20</th>\n","      <td>0.734</td>\n","      <td>0.726</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>50</th>\n","      <td>0.712</td>\n","      <td>0.724</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>100</th>\n","      <td>0.702</td>\n","      <td>0.729</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>200</th>\n","      <td>0.692</td>\n","      <td>0.730</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>400</th>\n","      <td>0.679</td>\n","      <td>0.721</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                  train PR-AUC  validation PR-AUC\n","min_samples_leaf                                 \n","1                        0.962              0.624\n","5                        0.800              0.705\n","10                       0.760              0.722\n","20                       0.734              0.726\n","50                       0.712              0.724\n","100                      0.702              0.729\n","200                      0.692              0.730\n","400                      0.679              0.721"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Chosen min_samples_leaf: 200\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n","\n","tuning = []\n","for leaf in [1, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 400]:\n","    rf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=300, min_samples_leaf=leaf, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n","    rf.fit(X_filled[\"train\"], y[\"train\"])\n","    tuning.append({\"min_samples_leaf\": leaf,\n","                   \"train PR-AUC\": average_precision_score(y[\"train\"], rf.predict_proba(X_filled[\"train\"])[:, 1]),\n","                   \"validation PR-AUC\": average_precision_score(y[\"validation\"], rf.predict_proba(X_filled[\"validation\"])[:, 1])})\n","tuning = pd.DataFrame(tuning).set_index(\"min_samples_leaf\").round(3)\n","display(tuning)\n","\n","ax = tuning.plot(marker=\"o\", logx=True, figsize=(8, 4))\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"PR-AUC\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Random forest: training vs validation PR-AUC by min_samples_leaf\")\n","plt.show()\n","\n","best_leaf = tuning[\"validation PR-AUC\"].idxmax()\n","print(\"Chosen min_samples_leaf:\", best_leaf)\n","\n","rf = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=300, min_samples_leaf=best_leaf, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n","rf.fit(X_filled[\"train\"], y[\"train\"])\n","rf_probs = {s: rf.predict_proba(X_filled[s])[:, 1] for s in SPLITS}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"dd5ea4a6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.045051,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.537138+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.492087+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **With no limit the forest memorises:** at `min_samples_leaf=1` the training PR-AUC is 0.962 but validation only 0.624, the large gap on the left of the plot. The trees learned rules for individual training rows that do not carry over to new seasons. This is overfitting, and it would make the forest worse than logistic regression (0.712).\n","2) **Larger leaves close the gap:** moving right in the plot, every rule has to cover more rows, so the training score (blue) falls and the validation score (orange) rises. From about 20 rows per leaf the two lines meet and stay close together, so the forest is no longer memorising.\n","3) **Too large is also bad:** at 400 the validation score drops again (0.721). The rules become so coarse that the forest starts to miss real patterns (underfitting).\n","4) **The best value is 200:** validation PR-AUC peaks at 0.730. The peak lies inside the range we tried, so a wider range would not find a better value.\n","5) **The exact choice matters little:** every value from 10 to 200 gives a validation PR-AUC between 0.722 and 0.730. With only 39 validation races, differences this small are within normal variation, so the important decision is to limit leaf size, not the exact number."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":80,"id":"6a60047f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.631561Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.630853Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.099246Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.098171Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.518162,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.101329+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:56.583167+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Accuracy</th>\n","      <th>ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>F1</th>\n","      <th>Precision</th>\n","      <th>Recall</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>train</th>\n","      <td>0.884</td>\n","      <td>0.934</td>\n","      <td>0.692</td>\n","      <td>0.666</td>\n","      <td>0.564</td>\n","      <td>0.813</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.905</td>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.730</td>\n","      <td>0.720</td>\n","      <td>0.646</td>\n","      <td>0.812</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.879</td>\n","      <td>0.937</td>\n","      <td>0.707</td>\n","      <td>0.671</td>\n","      <td>0.568</td>\n","      <td>0.819</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["            Accuracy  ROC-AUC  PR-AUC     F1  Precision  Recall  threshold\n","train          0.884    0.934   0.692  0.666      0.564   0.813       0.28\n","validation     0.905    0.930   0.730  0.720      0.646   0.812       0.28\n","test           0.879    0.937   0.707  0.671      0.568   0.819       0.28"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Validation scores with the usual 0.5 threshold instead: {'Accuracy': 0.91, 'ROC-AUC': 0.93, 'PR-AUC': 0.73, 'F1': 0.676, 'Precision': 0.737, 'Recall': 0.624}\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Validation scores so far:\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Accuracy</th>\n","      <th>ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>F1</th>\n","      <th>Precision</th>\n","      <th>Recall</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Logistic regression</th>\n","      <td>0.897</td>\n","      <td>0.927</td>\n","      <td>0.712</td>\n","      <td>0.699</td>\n","      <td>0.624</td>\n","      <td>0.795</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Random forest</th>\n","      <td>0.905</td>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.730</td>\n","      <td>0.720</td>\n","      <td>0.646</td>\n","      <td>0.812</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                     Accuracy  ROC-AUC  PR-AUC     F1  Precision  Recall  \\\n","Logistic regression     0.897    0.927   0.712  0.699      0.624   0.795   \n","Random forest           0.905    0.930   0.730  0.720      0.646   0.812   \n","\n","                     threshold  \n","Logistic regression       0.23  \n","Random forest             0.28  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["display(evaluate(\"Random forest\", rf_probs))\n","\n","threshold = results[\"Random forest\"][\"threshold\"].iloc[0]\n","print(\"Validation scores with the usual 0.5 threshold instead:\",\n","      {k: round(float(v), 3) for k, v in scores(y[\"validation\"], rf_probs[\"validation\"], 0.5).items()})\n","\n","cm = confusion_matrix(y[\"validation\"], (rf_probs[\"validation\"] >= threshold).astype(int))\n","sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\",\n","            xticklabels=[\"predicted no\", \"predicted podium\"], yticklabels=[\"really no\", \"really podium\"])\n","plt.title(f\"Random forest, validation seasons, threshold {threshold}\")\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"Validation scores so far:\")\n","display(pd.DataFrame({name: table.loc[\"validation\"] for name, table in results.items()}).T)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b12af634","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.046871,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.197244+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.150373+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","**1) Reading the confusion matrix (validation seasons, threshold 0.28)**\n","\n","| | Predicted no | Predicted podium |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **Really no podium** | 606 correct \"no\" (true negatives) | 52 false alarms (false positives) |\n","| **Really podium** | 22 missed podiums (false negatives) | 95 correct hits (true positives) |\n","\n","- **Precision = 95 / (95 + 52) = 0.646.** When the forest says \"podium\", it is right about 65% of the time.\n","- **Recall = 95 / (95 + 22) = 0.812.** It finds 95 of the 117 real podiums.\n","- **F1 = 0.720**, the balance of the two (2 × 0.646 × 0.812 / (0.646 + 0.812)).\n","- **Accuracy = (606 + 95) / 775 = 0.905**, only 5.6 points above always answering \"no\" (0.849), while F1 rises from 0 to 0.720. Accuracy is again not a useful comparison.\n","\n","The forest says \"podium\" 147 times (95 + 52) in 39 races, about 3.8 per race.\n","\n","**2) Compared with the baseline on the same validation seasons**\n","\n","| | Hits | Missed | False alarms | Precision | Recall | F1 | PR-AUC |\n","|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n","| Logistic regression | 93 | 24 | 56 | 0.624 | 0.795 | 0.699 | 0.712 |\n","| Random forest | 95 | 22 | 52 | 0.646 | 0.812 | 0.720 | 0.730 |\n","\n","The forest finds 2 more podiums and raises 4 fewer false alarms, so both precision and recall improve a little. Its PR-AUC is 0.018 higher. ROC-AUC is almost the same (0.930 against 0.927), so both models rank podium drivers above the others about equally well.\n","\n","**3) The threshold-free scores**\n","- **PR-AUC 0.730 against the no-skill level of 0.151**, almost five times higher.\n","- **ROC-AUC 0.930:** for a random podium driver and a random non-podium driver, the forest gives the podium driver the higher probability 93% of the time.\n","\n","**4) Why the threshold is 0.28 and not 0.5**\n","With 0.5 the forest is more careful: precision rises to 0.737 but recall falls to 0.624, so it misses many more podiums, and F1 drops to 0.676. At 0.28 F1 is 0.720. PR-AUC and ROC-AUC stay the same (0.730 and 0.930), because they do not depend on the threshold. The threshold was chosen on validation only.\n","\n","**5) No overfitting after tuning**\n","Training and validation are close (PR-AUC 0.692 against 0.730, ROC-AUC 0.934 against 0.930). Without the leaf limit, the gap was 0.962 against 0.624 (Cell 3).\n","\n","**6) On the unseen test seasons the gain disappears**\n","On 2022–2024 the forest scores PR-AUC 0.707 and F1 0.671, against 0.706 and 0.668 for logistic regression: practically equal. With the same threshold, recall stays high (0.819) but precision drops to 0.568, so the forest raises more false alarms in the new seasons than on validation. Its extra flexibility helps a little on validation but adds almost nothing on unseen data. With these six features, logistic regression already captures most of the signal.\n","\n","**7) Limitations**\n","A forest is much harder to read than logistic regression. There are no weights to inspect, only 300 trees of rules, which is why Lab 4 (p.9) calls it a black box. We explain it in Section 6 with permutation importance and SHAP. It also needed tuning: without the leaf limit it overfits badly."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"1c9ba2a5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.051094,"end_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.294109+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.243015+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4.4 Shallow neural network\n","\n","The brief requires a neural network with a shallow architecture of roughly 1–2 hidden layers, built with a standard library. We build it with Keras. The six scaled features from 3.8 enter the network, pass through the hidden layer(s), and come out as a single podium probability.\n","\n","**Choices fixed by the task.** These follow from the type of problem, not from results:\n","\n","| Choice | What we use | Why |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| Output layer | 1 neuron with a sigmoid | Our target is yes/no, so we need one probability between 0 and 1, which is exactly what the sigmoid gives. |\n","| Loss | Binary cross-entropy | The standard loss for a yes/no target. It punishes confident wrong answers most, e.g. a probability of 0.1 for a driver who did finish on the podium. |\n","| Hidden-layer activation | ReLU | Without an activation, stacked layers would still only add up the features in a straight line, like logistic regression. ReLU lets the network follow curved relationships, such as the steep drop in podium rate over the first grid positions seen in 3.3. |\n","| Optimizer | Adam | It adjusts the step size of each weight on its own, so it trains reliably without hand-tuning a learning rate. |\n","| Input | `scaled` | Networks train poorly when features have very different ranges (a rank from 1 to 27 against form from 0 to 1), which is why 3.8 standardised them. |\n","\n","**Protection against overfitting.** A network keeps improving on the training rows the longer it trains, and can start to memorise them. After every epoch (one pass over the training rows) we therefore measure the loss on the validation seasons. When it has not improved for 15 epochs, training stops and the weights from the best epoch are kept (early stopping). We watch the validation loss, not accuracy, because 4.1 showed that accuracy is misleading for our target. The validation data are our 2020–2021 seasons, so the split by season from 3.7 is kept. The training curve below shows whether this worked. The weights are updated after every 32 rows, training is capped at 200 epochs (early stopping ends it sooner), and a fixed random seed makes every run repeatable.\n","\n","**What we still have to decide.** The brief leaves the size of the network open, and we do not know in advance how much capacity our six features need. We therefore train three small networks (one hidden layer of 16 neurons, one of 32, and two hidden layers of 32 and 16) and choose the one with the highest validation PR-AUC, the same rule used for the random forest. The decision is made after the results, below."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":81,"id":"6bbe665e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.422771Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.421757Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:01:50.115795Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:01:50.11448Z"},"papermill":{"duration":112.753556,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:50.118428+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T18:59:57.364872+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\n","===== Training: 1 hidden layer (16) =====\n","Epoch 1/200\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["2026-10-19 19:00:18.320397: E external/local_xla/xla/stream_executor/cuda/cuda_platform.cc:51] failed call to cuInit: INTERNAL: CUDA error: Failed call to cuInit: UNKNOWN ERROR (303)\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[1m212/212\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m2s\u001b[0m 3ms/step - loss: 0.4873 - val_loss: 0.3599\n","Epoch 2/200\n","\u001b[1m212/212\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1s\u001b[0m 3ms/step - loss: 0.2954 - val_loss: 0.2764\n","Epoch 3/200\n","\u001b[1m212/212\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1s\u001b[0m 2ms/step - loss: 0.2525 - val_loss: 0.2568\n","Epoch 4/200\n","\u001b[1m212/212\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1s\u001b[0m 3ms/step - loss: 0.2400 - val_loss: 0.2491\n","Epoch 5/200\n","\u001b[1m212/212\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m\u001b[37m\u001b[0m \u001b[1m1s\u001b[0m 3ms/step - loss: 0.2346 - val_loss: 0.2451\n","Epoch 6/200\n","\u001b[1m212/212\u001b[0m \u001b[32m━━━