-color: #00af00\">260</span> (1.02 KB)\n","</pre>\n"],"text/plain":["\u001b[1m Optimizer params: \u001b[0m\u001b[38;5;34m260\u001b[0m (1.02 KB)\n"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1600x400 with 3 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["tuning[\"parameters\"] = [nets[name][0].count_params() for name in tuning.index]\n","display(tuning)\n","\n","best_arch = tuning[\"validation PR-AUC\"].idxmax()\n","print(\"Chosen architecture:\", best_arch)\n","nn, fit_log = nets[best_arch]\n","nn.summary()\n","nn_probs = {s: nn.predict(X_scaled[s], verbose=0).ravel() for s in SPLITS}\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(16, 4), sharey=True)\n","for ax, (name, (model, log)) in zip(axes, nets.items()):\n","    ax.plot(log.history[\"loss\"], label=\"Train\")\n","    ax.plot(log.history[\"val_loss\"], label=\"Validation\")\n","    ax.axvline(int(np.argmin(log.history[\"val_loss\"])), color=\"grey\", linestyle=\"--\", label=\"best epoch (weights kept)\")\n","    ax.set_title(name)\n","    ax.set_xlabel(\"Epoch\")\n","axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Binary cross-entropy loss\")\n","axes[0].legend()\n","plt.suptitle(\"Training curves of the three networks (train vs validation loss)\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b9628de5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.103623,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:51.74459+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:51.640967+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **All three networks score about the same:** validation PR-AUC is 0.736 for one hidden layer of 16 neurons, 0.736 for 32 neurons, and 0.735 for two hidden layers. More neurons or a second layer add nothing: six features do not need a large network.\n","2) **We choose one hidden layer of 16 neurons:** it shares the best validation score (0.736) with the 32-neuron network but has only 129 trainable weights, against 257 for 32 neurons and 769 for two hidden layers. When two options score the same, the smaller one is preferred, because it has fewer weights that could memorise the training seasons. (The summary also lists 260 optimizer parameters: these are values Adam keeps in memory during training, not part of the network.)\n","3) **Fewer epochs is not better:** the two-layer network stopped earliest (35 epochs), but that only says how long it trained, not how good it is. With six times more weights than the chosen network, it learned the training seasons faster, reached its best validation loss around epoch 20, and then started to get slightly worse on validation while still improving on training. That is the first sign of memorisation, and it also scores lowest (0.735). Each epoch takes about a second, so the time saved does not matter.\n","4) **How training went (curves):** in all three networks both losses drop steeply in the first few epochs and then flatten out, with only a small gap between training and validation. After the first epochs the improvements become tiny: the network has learned what the six features can tell it.\n","5) **Early stopping did its job:** the validation loss of the chosen network did not improve after epoch 47. After 15 more epochs without improvement, training stopped at epoch 62 (not the maximum of 200), and the weights from epoch 47 were kept. In the plot this is the dashed line, drawn at 46 because the plot counts epochs from 0 while the training log counts from 1. The other two networks behaved the same way: each stopped exactly 15 epochs after its best epoch.\n","6) **No overfitting in the chosen network:** its training and validation scores are close (PR-AUC 0.701 and 0.736).\n","7) **The optimizer settings work:** Adam was used with its default learning rate (0.001). The curves show this was suitable: the loss falls quickly and smoothly in the first epochs and then levels off. A learning rate that was too large would make the loss jump up and down, and one that was too small would make it fall slowly over many more epochs. Neither happens, so the learning rate was not tuned further."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":83,"id":"6309351e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:01:51.959567Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:01:51.95823Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.429185Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.428132Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.577701,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.431795+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:51.854094+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Accuracy</th>\n","      <th>ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>F1</th>\n","      <th>Precision</th>\n","      <th>Recall</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>train</th>\n","      <td>0.902</td>\n","      <td>0.934</td>\n","      <td>0.701</td>\n","      <td>0.670</td>\n","      <td>0.641</td>\n","      <td>0.702</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.911</td>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.736</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.703</td>\n","      <td>0.709</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.899</td>\n","      <td>0.939</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.673</td>\n","      <td>0.660</td>\n","      <td>0.686</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["            Accuracy  ROC-AUC  PR-AUC     F1  Precision  Recall  threshold\n","train          0.902    0.934   0.701  0.670      0.641   0.702       0.41\n","validation     0.911    0.930   0.736  0.706      0.703   0.709       0.41\n","test           0.899    0.939   0.706  0.673      0.660   0.686       0.41"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Validation scores with the usual 0.5 threshold instead: {'Accuracy': 0.908, 'ROC-AUC': 0.93, 'PR-AUC': 0.736, 'F1': 0.682, 'Precision': 0.717, 'Recall': 0.65}\n"]},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Validation scores so far:\n"]},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>Accuracy</th>\n","      <th>ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>F1</th>\n","      <th>Precision</th>\n","      <th>Recall</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Logistic regression</th>\n","      <td>0.897</td>\n","      <td>0.927</td>\n","      <td>0.712</td>\n","      <td>0.699</td>\n","      <td>0.624</td>\n","      <td>0.795</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Random forest</th>\n","      <td>0.905</td>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.730</td>\n","      <td>0.720</td>\n","      <td>0.646</td>\n","      <td>0.812</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>Neural network</th>\n","      <td>0.911</td>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.736</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.703</td>\n","      <td>0.709</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                     Accuracy  ROC-AUC  PR-AUC     F1  Precision  Recall  \\\n","Logistic regression     0.897    0.927   0.712  0.699      0.624   0.795   \n","Random forest           0.905    0.930   0.730  0.720      0.646   0.812   \n","Neural network          0.911    0.930   0.736  0.706      0.703   0.709   \n","\n","                     threshold  \n","Logistic regression       0.23  \n","Random forest             0.28  \n","Neural network            0.41  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["display(evaluate(\"Neural network\", nn_probs))\n","\n","threshold = results[\"Neural network\"][\"threshold\"].iloc[0]\n","print(\"Validation scores with the usual 0.5 threshold instead:\",\n","      {k: round(float(v), 3) for k, v in scores(y[\"validation\"], nn_probs[\"validation\"], 0.5).items()})\n","\n","cm = confusion_matrix(y[\"validation\"], (nn_probs[\"validation\"] >= threshold).astype(int))\n","sns.heatmap(cm, annot=True, fmt=\"d\", cmap=\"Blues\",\n","            xticklabels=[\"predicted no\", \"predicted podium\"], yticklabels=[\"really no\", \"really podium\"])\n","plt.title(f\"Neural network, validation seasons, threshold {threshold}\")\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"Validation scores so far:\")\n","display(pd.DataFrame({name: table.loc[\"validation\"] for name, table in results.items()}).T)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"65f7f9ff","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.111509,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.65947+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.547961+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","**1) Reading the confusion matrix (validation seasons, threshold 0.41)**\n","\n","| | Predicted no | Predicted podium |\n","|---|---|---|\n","| **Really no podium** | 623 correct \"no\" (true negatives) | 35 false alarms (false positives) |\n","| **Really podium** | 34 missed podiums (false negatives) | 83 correct hits (true positives) |\n","\n","- **Precision = 83 / (83 + 35) = 0.703.** When the network says \"podium\", it is right 70% of the time, the highest of all models.\n","- **Recall = 83 / (83 + 34) = 0.709.** It finds 83 of the 117 real podiums, the lowest of all models.\n","- **F1 = 0.706** (2 × 0.703 × 0.709 / (0.703 + 0.709)).\n","- **Accuracy = (623 + 83) / 775 = 0.911.** The highest so far, but as shown in 4.1 this mostly reflects the many correct \"no\" answers.\n","\n","It says \"podium\" 118 times (83 + 35) in 39 races, about 3.0 per race, almost exactly the 3 real podium places. Its precision and recall are nearly equal.\n","\n","**2) Compared with the other models on validation**\n","\n","| | Hits | Missed | False alarms | Precision | Recall | F1 | PR-AUC |\n","|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n","| Logistic regression | 93 | 24 | 56 | 0.624 | 0.795 | 0.699 | 0.712 |\n","| Random forest | 95 | 22 | 52 | 0.646 | 0.812 | 0.720 | 0.730 |\n","| Neural network | 83 | 34 | 35 | 0.703 | 0.709 | 0.706 | 0.736 |\n","\n","The network has the highest PR-AUC (0.736), so it ranks podium drivers above the others slightly better than the other models. At its threshold it makes a different trade-off: far fewer false alarms (35 against 52–56) but more missed podiums (34 against 22–24). Its F1 lies between the baseline and the forest.\n","\n","**3) The threshold-free scores**\n","- **PR-AUC 0.736 against the no-skill level of 0.151**, almost five times higher.\n","- **ROC-AUC 0.930:** for a random podium driver and a random non-podium driver, the network gives the podium driver the higher probability 93% of the time, the same as the forest.\n","\n","**4) Why the threshold is 0.41**\n","The network's best threshold is higher than for the other models (0.23 and 0.28), because its probabilities are spread differently. With 0.5 it misses more podiums (recall 0.650) and F1 drops to 0.682. PR-AUC and ROC-AUC stay the same (0.736 and 0.930), because they do not depend on the threshold. The threshold was chosen on validation only.\n","\n","**5) No overfitting**\n","Training and validation are close (PR-AUC 0.701 and 0.736, ROC-AUC 0.934 and 0.930), which confirms the training curves.\n","\n","**6) On the unseen test seasons**\n","PR-AUC is 0.706 and F1 0.673, practically the same as logistic regression (0.706 and 0.668) and the forest (0.707 and 0.671). Its small lead on validation does not carry over to 2022–2024. As with the random forest, the extra flexibility of the network does not beat the baseline on unseen seasons.\n","\n","**7) Limitations**\n","The network is a black box: its 129 weights cannot be read like the logistic regression weights, so it is explained in Section 6. Its result also depends on the random starting weights. We fix them with a seed"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"cef3563a","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.103016,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.868358+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.765342+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4.5 Model comparison\n","\n","All models were trained on the same rows and the same six features, their settings and thresholds were chosen on the validation seasons only, and every one was scored on the unseen test seasons with the same metrics. This section puts the results side by side, plots the ROC and precision-recall curves of all models, and chooses the final model."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":84,"id":"8bbd94b7","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.099659Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.099112Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.118333Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.117388Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.138896,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.120501+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:52.981605+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>F1</th>\n","      <th>Precision</th>\n","      <th>Recall</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>model</th>\n","      <th>split</th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th></th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\">Logistic regression</th>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.927</td>\n","      <td>0.712</td>\n","      <td>0.699</td>\n","      <td>0.624</td>\n","      <td>0.795</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.935</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.668</td>\n","      <td>0.545</td>\n","      <td>0.863</td>\n","      <td>0.23</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\">Random forest</th>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.730</td>\n","      <td>0.720</td>\n","      <td>0.646</td>\n","      <td>0.812</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.937</td>\n","      <td>0.707</td>\n","      <td>0.671</td>\n","      <td>0.568</td>\n","      <td>0.819</td>\n","      <td>0.28</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th rowspan=\"2\" valign=\"top\">Neural network</th>\n","      <th>validation</th>\n","      <td>0.930</td>\n","      <td>0.736</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.703</td>\n","      <td>0.709</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>test</th>\n","      <td>0.939</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.673</td>\n","      <td>0.660</td>\n","      <td>0.686</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                                ROC-AUC  PR-AUC     F1  Precision  Recall  \\\n","model               split                                                   \n","Logistic regression validation    0.927   0.712  0.699      0.624   0.795   \n","                    test          0.935   0.706  0.668      0.545   0.863   \n","Random forest       validation    0.930   0.730  0.720      0.646   0.812   \n","                    test          0.937   0.707  0.671      0.568   0.819   \n","Neural network      validation    0.930   0.736  0.706      0.703   0.709   \n","                    test          0.939   0.706  0.673      0.660   0.686   \n","\n","                                threshold  \n","model               split                  \n","Logistic regression validation       0.23  \n","                    test             0.23  \n","Random forest       validation       0.28  \n","                    test             0.28  \n","Neural network      validation       0.41  \n","                    test             0.41  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["models = [\"Logistic regression\", \"Random forest\", \"Neural network\"]\n","comparison = pd.concat({name: results[name].loc[[\"validation\", \"test\"]] for name in models})\n","comparison.index.names = [\"model\", \"split\"]\n","display(comparison.drop(columns=\"Accuracy\"))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"83fe4474","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.107706,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.331213+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.223507+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Every model is far above the floor:** on the test seasons all three reach a PR-AUC of about 0.71 and a ROC-AUC of about 0.94, against the no-skill levels of 0.151 and 0.5.\n","2) **On validation the more flexible models are slightly ahead:** PR-AUC 0.736 for the neural network and 0.730 for the random forest, against 0.712 for logistic regression. The forest has the best F1 (0.720).\n","3) **On the unseen test seasons the three are practically equal:** PR-AUC 0.706, 0.707 and 0.706, and F1 between 0.668 and 0.673. The small leads seen on validation do not carry over. Validation contains only 39 races, so differences of about 0.02 there are within normal variation.\n","4) **They differ mainly in their trade-off, not in their skill:** logistic regression, with the lowest threshold (0.23), finds the most podiums on test (recall 0.863) but raises the most false alarms (precision 0.545). The neural network, with the highest threshold (0.41), is the most careful (precision 0.660, recall 0.686). The forest lies in between. F1 balances the two and ends up almost the same for all three.\n","5) **All scores drop a little from validation to test** (for example the network's PR-AUC from 0.736 to 0.706). The test seasons 2022–2024 follow new car rules, so a small drop is expected. The drop is small, so what the models learned from 2003–2019 still largely holds."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":85,"id":"2ed7ed66","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.557795Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.557396Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.023788Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.0228Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.583918,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.02734+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:53.443422+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x500 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["from sklearn.metrics import roc_curve, precision_recall_curve\n","\n","all_probs = {\"Logistic regression\": lr_probs, \"Random forest\": rf_probs, \"Neural network\": nn_probs}\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n","for name, probs in all_probs.items():\n","    fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y[\"test\"], probs[\"test\"])\n","    axes[0].plot(fpr, tpr, label=f\"{name} (ROC-AUC {results[name].loc['test', 'ROC-AUC']:.3f})\")\n","    prec, rec, _ = precision_recall_curve(y[\"test\"], probs[\"test\"])\n","    axes[1].plot(rec, prec, label=f\"{name} (PR-AUC {results[name].loc['test', 'PR-AUC']:.3f})\")\n","axes[0].plot([0, 1], [0, 1], \"k--\", label=\"coin flip (0.5)\")\n","axes[1].axhline(y[\"test\"].mean(), color=\"k\", linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"no skill ({y['test'].mean():.3f})\")\n","axes[0].set(title=\"ROC curve, test seasons 2022-2024\", xlabel=\"Share of non-podium drivers wrongly flagged\",\n","            ylabel=\"Share of podiums found (recall)\")\n","axes[1].set(title=\"Precision-recall curve, test seasons 2022-2024\", xlabel=\"Share of podiums found (recall)\",\n","            ylabel=\"Share of podium calls that are right (precision)\")\n","axes[0].legend(loc=\"lower right\")\n","axes[1].legend(loc=\"lower left\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"97bdcf88","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.106025,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.242078+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.136053+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","**How to read the two plots.** A model gives every driver a podium probability. Each point on a curve is what happens for one threshold: lowering the threshold flags more drivers as \"podium\", so the curve moves to the right. The area under each curve is the ROC-AUC and PR-AUC in the table.\n","\n","1) **ROC curve (left):**\n","   - The x-axis is the share of non-podium drivers the model wrongly flags as \"podium\" (false alarms). The y-axis is the share of real podiums it finds (recall).\n","   - A good model finds many podiums before raising many false alarms, so its curve shoots up and hugs the top-left corner. The dashed diagonal is what guessing at random (a coin flip) would give.\n","   - All three models rise steeply. On the test seasons, while wrongly flagging only 10% of the non-podium drivers, they already find about 80% of the podiums. At 20% false alarms they find about 93%.\n","\n","2) **Precision-recall curve (right):**\n","   - The x-axis is again the share of podiums found (recall). The y-axis is the share of the model's podium calls that are right (precision).\n","   - A good model stays precise while it finds more and more podiums, so its curve stays high as it moves right. The dashed line at 0.151 is the no-skill level: a model that flags drivers at random would be right only as often as podiums occur.\n","   - While the models find the first 40% of the podiums, about 77% of their podium calls are right. These are the clear favourites, such as front-row starters in top teams. To find 80% of the podiums, precision falls to about 55%: the remaining podiums come from drivers starting further back, and to catch them the models must also flag many drivers who do not make it.\n","   - The zigzag at the far left comes from the very first calls, where a single right or wrong call changes precision a lot. It has little effect on the area.\n","\n","3) **The three lines lie almost on top of each other in both plots.** Across all thresholds the models rank drivers in nearly the same order, so they are equally good at separating podium finishers from the rest. This is the visual version of the table: on the test seasons ROC-AUC is 0.935–0.939 and PR-AUC 0.706–0.707 for all three, far above the coin-flip and no-skill lines.\n","\n","**Final model choice**\n","\n","Our rule, fixed before training, is to compare models on the primary metric, PR-AUC, on the validation seasons. By that rule the **neural network is our final model** (0.736, against 0.730 for the random forest and 0.712 for logistic regression). It is used in the experiments, the explanations and the inference function that follow.\n","\n","We report its advantage honestly: it is small on validation and disappears on the test seasons, where all three models score the same and their curves overlap. Compared with the baseline, the extra complexity of the forest and the network gives little gain with these six features. The baseline already captures most of what the features can tell us, so the limit is set by the information in the features rather than by the choice of model."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"333e728c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.105719,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.454407+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.348688+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["---\n","# 5. Experiments\n","\n","Section 3 chose every feature using evidence from before training. This section measures, after training, what each choice actually contributes. Every experiment retrains the final model from 4.4 (one hidden layer of 16 neurons, the same seed, early stopping on the validation seasons) and changes only one thing. As in Section 4, the threshold is chosen on the validation seasons, and the test seasons are only scored.\n","\n","1) **Feature-group ablation (5.1):** remove one feature group at a time and retrain.\n","2) **Preprocessing-order experiments (5.2–5.3):** change the order of the preparation steps from 3.8.\n","\n","One thing to keep in mind when reading the results: with only 39 validation races, differences of about 0.01–0.02 in PR-AUC are within normal variation (4.3, 4.5). Only larger drops show a real effect."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":86,"id":"7ad7e75d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.667559Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.666986Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.678546Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.677644Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.121931,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.680684+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.558753+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def train_net(X_tr, y_tr, X_va, y_va):\n","    \"\"\"The final architecture from 4.4, trained exactly as there (seed 42, early stopping on validation loss).\"\"\"\n","    keras.utils.set_random_seed(42)\n","    model = keras.Sequential([layers.Input(shape=(X_tr.shape[1],))]\n","                             + [layers.Dense(n, activation=\"relu\") for n in architectures[best_arch]]\n","                             + [layers.Dense(1, activation=\"sigmoid\")])\n","    model.compile(optimizer=\"adam\", loss=\"binary_crossentropy\")\n","    model.fit(X_tr, y_tr, validation_data=(X_va, y_va), epochs=200, batch_size=32, verbose=0,\n","              callbacks=[EarlyStopping(monitor=\"val_loss\", patience=15, restore_best_weights=True)])\n","    return model\n","\n","def run(name, X, cols=FEATURES):\n","    \"\"\"Train on X['train'][cols], choose the threshold on validation, score validation and test.\"\"\"\n","    net = train_net(X[\"train\"][cols], y[\"train\"], X[\"validation\"][cols], y[\"validation\"])\n","    probs = {s: net.predict(X[s][cols], verbose=0).ravel() for s in SPLITS}\n","    t = best_threshold(y[\"validation\"], probs[\"validation\"])\n","    return {\"experiment\": name,\n","            \"validation PR-AUC\": average_precision_score(y[\"validation\"], probs[\"validation\"]),\n","            \"test PR-AUC\": average_precision_score(y[\"test\"], probs[\"test\"]),\n","            \"validation F1\": f1_score(y[\"validation\"], probs[\"validation\"] >= t),\n","            \"test F1\": f1_score(y[\"test\"], probs[\"test\"] >= t),\n","            \"test ROC-AUC\": roc_auc_score(y[\"test\"], probs[\"test\"]),\n","            \"threshold\": t}"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e667dde0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.104619,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.890744+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.786125+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5.1 Feature-group ablation\n","\n","We remove one of the four groups from 3.7 (grid, qualifying, standings, form), retrain the network on the remaining features, and measure how much PR-AUC drops compared with the full model. Section 3 showed that grid and qualifying overlap almost completely (0.97), so removing only one of them may cost little because the other stands in for it.\n","\n","The first row retrains the full model with the same helper. It should reproduce the network from 4.4 (validation PR-AUC 0.736, test 0.706), which confirms that every other row differs only by the removed features."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":87,"id":"27165c36","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:01:55.106509Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:01:55.106015Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.082433Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.081368Z"},"papermill":{"duration":261.085656,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.084417+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:01:54.998761+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>validation PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>test PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>validation F1</th>\n","      <th>test F1</th>\n","      <th>test ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","      <th>validation PR-AUC drop</th>\n","      <th>test PR-AUC drop</th>\n","    </tr>\n","   