0.681   \n","without standings               0.733        0.705          0.715    0.672   \n","without form                    0.726        0.710          0.708    0.662   \n","\n","                    test ROC-AUC  threshold  validation PR-AUC drop  \\\n","experiment                                                            \n","all six features           0.939       0.41                   0.000   \n","without grid               0.936       0.39                   0.007   \n","without qualifying         0.940       0.23                   0.016   \n","without standings          0.938       0.26                   0.003   \n","without form               0.938       0.41                   0.010   \n","\n","                    test PR-AUC drop  \n","experiment                            \n","all six features               0.000  \n","without grid                   0.001  \n","without qualifying            -0.009  \n","without standings              0.001  \n","without form                  -0.004  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 900x400 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["ablation_runs = {f\"without {g}\": [f for f in FEATURES if f not in cols] for g, cols in FEATURE_GROUPS.items()}\n","\n","ablation = [run(\"all six features\", X_scaled)]\n","for name, kept in ablation_runs.items():\n","    ablation.append(run(name, X_scaled, kept))\n","ablation = pd.DataFrame(ablation).set_index(\"experiment\")\n","for split in [\"validation\", \"test\"]:\n","    ablation[f\"{split} PR-AUC drop\"] = ablation.loc[\"all six features\", f\"{split} PR-AUC\"] - ablation[f\"{split} PR-AUC\"]\n","display(ablation.round(3))\n","\n","drops = ablation.drop(\"all six features\")[[\"validation PR-AUC drop\", \"test PR-AUC drop\"]]\n","ax = drops.iloc[::-1].plot.barh(figsize=(9, 4))\n","ax.axvline(0, color=\"black\", linewidth=0.8)\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"drop in PR-AUC compared with all six features (higher = the group mattered more)\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Feature-group ablation, neural network\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6c56921f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.116593,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.32322+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.206627+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **The reference run reproduces the final model exactly:** with all six features the helper gives the same scores as the network in 4.4 (validation PR-AUC 0.736, test 0.706, threshold 0.41). Every other row therefore differs only in the features removed.\n","2) **No single group is indispensable:** removing grid, qualifying, standings or form one at a time lowers the validation PR-AUC by only 0.003–0.016. On test the changes are between −0.009 and +0.001, and removing qualifying or form even scores slightly higher. With 39 validation races these differences are within normal variation (4.5), so none of the four groups is needed on its own.\n","3) **Because the groups overlap, each one can stand in for another:** grid and qualifying are almost the same (0.97, heatmap in 3.8), and form and standings both describe how strong a driver and team have been. When one group is removed, the model gets most of the same information from another.\n","4) **What the ablation adds to Section 3:** Section 3 showed before training that every group is linked to a podium. The ablation shows after training that no group is needed on its own, because the groups carry overlapping information. We keep all six features: removing any one group does not improve the model, and the overlap lets the model still work when some values are missing (Section 7)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"61528e14","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.111443,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.544242+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.432799+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5.2 Preprocessing order A: split first, or prepare first?\n","\n","In 3.8 we split the seasons first and then learned the fill values (training medians) and the scaling (training mean and standard deviation) from the training seasons only. The alternative order prepares first: medians, mean and standard deviation are computed on all 2003–2024 rows, and the data is split afterwards. That lets the validation and test seasons influence the preparation, a mild form of leakage. We run both orders and compare."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":88,"id":"17dbfdce","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.769656Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.769003Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.065918Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.064957Z"},"papermill":{"duration":34.521214,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.177808+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:16.656594+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>median (train only)</th>\n","      <th>median (all rows)</th>\n","      <th>mean (train only)</th>\n","      <th>mean (all rows)</th>\n","      <th>std (train only)</th>\n","      <th>std (all rows)</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>grid_pos</th>\n","      <td>11.0</td>\n","      <td>11.0</td>\n","      <td>11.180</td>\n","      <td>11.023</td>\n","      <td>6.234</td>\n","      <td>6.138</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>quali_pos</th>\n","      <td>11.0</td>\n","      <td>11.0</td>\n","      <td>11.178</td>\n","      <td>11.013</td>\n","      <td>6.234</td>\n","      <td>6.131</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>driver_rank_before</th>\n","      <td>11.0</td>\n","      <td>11.0</td>\n","      <td>11.252</td>\n","      <td>11.109</td>\n","      <td>6.223</td>\n","      <td>6.130</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>team_rank_before</th>\n","      <td>6.0</td>\n","      <td>6.0</td>\n","      <td>5.838</td>\n","      <td>5.764</td>\n","      <td>3.019</td>\n","      <td>2.973</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>driver_form</th>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.141</td>\n","      <td>0.144</td>\n","      <td>0.254</td>\n","      <td>0.255</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>team_form</th>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.0</td>\n","      <td>0.143</td>\n","      <td>0.144</td>\n","      <td>0.231</td>\n","      <td>0.231</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                    median (train only)  median (all rows)  mean (train only)  \\\n","grid_pos                           11.0               11.0             11.180   \n","quali_pos                          11.0               11.0             11.178   \n","driver_rank_before                 11.0               11.0             11.252   \n","team_rank_before                    6.0                6.0              5.838   \n","driver_form                         0.0                0.0              0.141   \n","team_form                           0.0                0.0              0.143   \n","\n","                    mean (all rows)  std (train only)  std (all rows)  \n","grid_pos                     11.023             6.234           6.138  \n","quali_pos                    11.013             6.234           6.131  \n","driver_rank_before           11.109             6.223           6.130  \n","team_rank_before              5.764             3.019           2.973  \n","driver_form                   0.144             0.254           0.255  \n","team_form                     0.144             0.231           0.231  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        vertical-align: middle;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n","        vertical-align: top;\n","    }\n","\n","    .dataframe thead th {\n","        text-align: right;\n","    }\n","</style>\n","<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n","  <thead>\n","    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n","      <th></th>\n","      <th>validation PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>test PR-AUC</th>\n","      <th>validation F1</th>\n","      <th>test F1</th>\n","      <th>test ROC-AUC</th>\n","      <th>threshold</th>\n","    </tr>\n","  </thead>\n","  <tbody>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>split → prepare (ours, 3.8)</th>\n","      <td>0.736</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.673</td>\n","      <td>0.939</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>prepare → split</th>\n","      <td>0.735</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.706</td>\n","      <td>0.673</td>\n","      <td>0.939</td>\n","      <td>0.41</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["                             validation PR-AUC  test PR-AUC  validation F1  \\\n","split → prepare (ours, 3.8)              0.736        0.706          0.706   \n","prepare → split                          0.735        0.706          0.706   \n","\n","                             test F1  test ROC-AUC  threshold  \n","split → prepare (ours, 3.8)    0.673         0.939       0.41  \n","prepare → split                0.673         0.939       0.41  "]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["def fill_with(df, medians):\n","    \"\"\"The 3.8 fill rule with chosen medians: qualifying gap -> grid position, other gaps -> the median.\"\"\"\n","    df = df.copy()\n","    df[\"quali_pos\"] = df[\"quali_pos\"].fillna(df[\"grid_pos\"])\n","    df[FEATURES] = df[FEATURES].fillna(medians)\n","    return df\n","\n","# alternative order: learn medians and scaling on ALL 2003-2024 rows, then split\n","filled_all = fill_with(model_table, model_table[FEATURES].median())\n","scaler_all = StandardScaler().fit(filled_all[FEATURES])\n","X_prepare_first = {s: pd.DataFrame(scaler_all.transform(filled_all.loc[filled_all[\"split\"] == s, FEATURES]),\n","                                   columns=FEATURES, index=filled_all.index[filled_all[\"split\"] == s]) for s in SPLITS}\n","\n","display(pd.DataFrame({\"median (train only)\": MEDIANS, \"median (all rows)\": model_table[FEATURES].median(),\n","                      \"mean (train only)\": scaler.mean_, \"mean (all rows)\": scaler_all.mean_,\n","                      \"std (train only)\": scaler.scale_, \"std (all rows)\": scaler_all.scale_}).round(3))\n","\n","exp_a = pd.DataFrame([ablation.loc[\"all six features\"].rename(\"split → prepare (ours, 3.8)\"),\n","                      pd.Series(run(\"prepare → split\", X_prepare_first)).drop(\"experiment\").rename(\"prepare → split\")])\n","display(exp_a[[\"validation PR-AUC\", \"test PR-AUC\", \"validation F1\", \"test F1\", \"test ROC-AUC\", \"threshold\"]].astype(float).round(3))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"809270c4","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.242623,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.53003+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.287407+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**What we notice**\n","\n","1) **Preparing on all rows changes the numbers only slightly:** the medians are identical (11, 11, 11, 6, 0, 0), and the means and standard deviations move a little. For example the grid mean is 11.18 on training seasons and 11.02 on all rows, because the later seasons have smaller fields of 20 cars.\n","2) **The model does not notice:** validation PR-AUC is 0.735 against 0.736, and every test score is identical (PR-AUC 0.706, F1 0.673, ROC-AUC 0.939).\n","3) **Why the leakage is small here:** the training seasons are 76% of the rows, and the later seasons look much like them, so including them barely shifts the preparation. With a feature whose distribution changed more over time, the effect would be larger.\n","\n","**Our decision:** we keep split → prepare. It is the correct order, because at prediction time the future seasons are unknown. The experiment shows that our results do not depend on this choice."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"465928f0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.111816,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.750472+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.638656+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5.3 Preprocessing order B: fill then scale, or scale then fill?\n","\n","In 3.8 we filled the gaps first and scaled afterwards. The other order scales first, computing the mean and standard deviation from the training values that exist and ignoring the gaps, and fills the gaps afterwards with the same rule applied on the scaled values. The fill values themselves are the same in both orders, but the scaling is learned from different numbers: with fill-then-scale, the filled values are part of the mean and standard deviation; with scale-then-fill, they are not. We check how this changes the training distributions and whether the model notices."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":89,"id":"89345b56","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.971481Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.970777Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T19:07:30.642866Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T19:07:30.64186Z"},"papermill":{"duration":38.896613,"end_time":"2026-10-19T19:07:30.755469+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T19:06:51.858856+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/html":["<div>\n","<style scoped>\n","    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n","        